WEBVTT

01:18.578 --> 01:21.331
BASED ON THE TRUE STORY OF GO PLAYERS
CHO HOON-HYUN AND LEE CHANG-HO

01:21.414 --> 01:24.000
ALL CHARACTERS AND EVENTS
MAY DIFFER FROM REAL-LIFE COUNTERPARTS

01:25.585 --> 01:27.670
THE YING SHIBEI WORLD GO CHAMPIONSHIP
WAS HELD IN THE 1980S

01:27.754 --> 01:28.922
TO FIND THE CHAMPION OF THE WORLD

01:29.005 --> 01:30.840
A SINGLE SPOT WAS GIVEN TO KOREA,
AN UNDERDOG COUNTRY

01:30.924 --> 01:33.093
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN
ADVANCED TO THE FINAL AGAINST EXPECTATIONS

01:33.176 --> 01:35.678
HIS OPPONENT, NIE WEIPING 9-DAN OF CHINA,
KNOWN AS "THE BLACK BEAR OF THE CONTINENT"

01:35.762 --> 01:37.680
WON THE CHINA-JAPAN SUPER LEAGUE
11 CONSECUTIVE TIMES

01:37.764 --> 01:38.932
AND WAS THE WORLD'S BEST PLAYER

01:39.015 --> 01:40.058
[dramatic music playing]

01:40.141 --> 01:44.687
[announcer 1] The final of the first Ying
Shibei World Professional Go Championship

01:44.771 --> 01:47.065
will be held in Singapore today.

01:47.148 --> 01:50.985
Korea's Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan
and China's Nie Weiping 9-dan,

01:51.069 --> 01:53.029
tying at two wins, two losses each,

01:53.113 --> 01:55.073
will fight in this match of the century

01:55.156 --> 01:57.992
to become king
of the international Go scene.

01:58.076 --> 02:00.745
White has won
in all the previous matches played,

02:00.829 --> 02:04.958
so there is great interest already in
who will play white in the final match.

02:05.041 --> 02:06.584
-[clicking]
-[reporter 1] Champion Cho!

02:06.668 --> 02:08.461
[reporter 2] Are you going
to attack fiercely?

02:08.545 --> 02:09.379
[reporter 1] Mr. Cho!

02:09.462 --> 02:12.048
[reporter 3] What have you done
to prepare for the match today?

02:12.132 --> 02:13.925
-[clamoring continues]
-Sir!

02:14.008 --> 02:15.343
[clamoring]

02:15.426 --> 02:18.346
-Champion Cho!
-[crowd chanting] Nie Weiping!

02:18.429 --> 02:19.848
[reporter 4] How do you feel now?

02:19.931 --> 02:20.849
[in Chinese] Piss off to Korea!

02:20.932 --> 02:24.102
[crowd] Nie Weiping! Nie Weiping!

02:24.185 --> 02:27.605
China will definitely win!
China will definitely win!

02:27.689 --> 02:29.941
MATCH VENUE
STAMFORD HOTEL, SINGAPORE

02:30.441 --> 02:32.610
[anticipatory music playing]

02:39.659 --> 02:41.870
[judge in Japanese]
Nie Weiping 9-dan, white.

02:41.953 --> 02:44.372
Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan, black.

02:44.455 --> 02:46.541
[music continues]

02:50.503 --> 02:52.005
[oxygen hissing]

02:52.088 --> 02:53.464
[inhales]

02:55.675 --> 02:56.509
[grunts]

02:59.304 --> 03:01.222
[in Japanese] Let the match begin.

03:01.306 --> 03:03.141
[music continues]

03:03.224 --> 03:05.602
THE 1ST YING SHIBEI
WORLD GO CHAMPIONSHIP FINAL, LAST ROUND

03:05.685 --> 03:08.688
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS NIE WEIPING 9-DAN

03:18.281 --> 03:19.157
[lighter clicks]

03:19.240 --> 03:20.783
[music continues]

03:32.295 --> 03:35.548
[music intensifies]

03:36.507 --> 03:41.346
THE MATCH

03:41.429 --> 03:43.181
[in English] Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan

03:43.264 --> 03:45.934
has ascended
to the top of the international Go scene.

03:46.017 --> 03:47.769
[reporter] Cho 9-dan defeated Japan,

03:47.852 --> 03:49.896
who has boasted to be the center
of the Go scene,

03:49.979 --> 03:53.024
and also defeated China,
where Go first originated.

03:53.650 --> 03:55.193
His victory excitingly proves

03:55.276 --> 03:58.238
that the quality of Korea's Go
is at the top of the world.

03:58.321 --> 03:59.864
[Hoon-hyun] Right now, well,

04:00.490 --> 04:04.452
perhaps I would not even lose
to the supreme god of Go himself. [laughs]

04:04.535 --> 04:07.163
[reporter 1] Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan,
the Go world champion,

04:07.247 --> 04:08.414
returned to Korea today,

04:08.498 --> 04:11.501
participating in a car parade
from Gimpo Airport

04:11.584 --> 04:13.586
to the Korea Baduk Association
in Jongno 2-ga.

04:13.670 --> 04:15.588
[reporter 2] The government
awarded Cho 9-dan

04:15.672 --> 04:17.799
with the Eungwan Order of Culture Merit

04:17.882 --> 04:21.386
for improving the prestige of Korea's Go
throughout the world.

04:22.845 --> 04:26.766
5 MONTHS LATER

04:26.849 --> 04:30.853
ONE-ON-MANY TEACHING MATCH
WITH PROFESSIONAL GO PLAYERS

04:31.896 --> 04:32.855
[stones clattering]

04:35.817 --> 04:37.402
-[man 1] The boy's amazing.
-[boy sighs]

04:37.485 --> 04:40.071
He solved the life-and-death problem.

04:40.154 --> 04:41.698
-[man 2] Huh?
-[man 1] Huh? Right?

04:41.781 --> 04:43.741
-Earlier…
-Hey, hey. Hey, go.

04:45.243 --> 04:46.119
-Okay.
-Hmm?

04:46.202 --> 04:47.412
-Let's go.
-Uh-huh.

04:47.495 --> 04:50.873
Hey, you're in a tight spot,
Pro Cheon. [chuckles softly]

04:50.957 --> 04:52.834
He's giving you a hard time, huh?

04:52.917 --> 04:55.503
[man 3] This kid's a Go prodigy in Jeonju.

04:55.586 --> 04:57.839
He's been playing
for less than half a year.

04:57.922 --> 05:01.009
Right, I heard there's no one
who could beat him in Jeonju…

05:01.092 --> 05:03.761
-No, in Jeollanam-do, right? Ha!
-[man 4] He really must be a prodigy.

05:03.845 --> 05:05.972
I think it's over. Wanna stop?

05:07.557 --> 05:08.599
[Pro Cheon] Just wait.

05:11.269 --> 05:12.186
[Pro Cheon scoffs]

05:12.270 --> 05:13.438
It's not over yet.

05:13.521 --> 05:14.439
What?

05:15.773 --> 05:18.151
It's over. It's obvious.

05:18.234 --> 05:20.069
Mind if I step in for him?

05:22.030 --> 05:24.365
-This is it!
-[men laugh]

05:24.449 --> 05:26.200
[mysterious music playing]

05:38.921 --> 05:40.506
[man 1] Oh, it's an atari.

05:40.590 --> 05:42.467
ATARI: OPPONENT'S STONE
CAPTURED ON THE NEXT MOVE

05:42.550 --> 05:44.302
[man 1] Looks like
he's been hit really hard.

05:44.385 --> 05:45.887
Should we call it a tie and stop here?

05:45.970 --> 05:48.014
[music continues]

05:51.351 --> 05:53.728
[man 4] Wow, he's amazing.

05:53.811 --> 05:56.230
Champion Cho is Korea's best.
I can't believe it!

05:57.106 --> 05:58.858
[man 1] He's champion for a reason.

06:00.693 --> 06:03.529
It's much harder to win
when you're given the advantage.

06:06.908 --> 06:09.285
You stepped in
when I was going easy. [chuckles]

06:09.369 --> 06:11.079
Hey, wait! Play another one!

06:11.162 --> 06:12.622
Oh, what are you doing?

06:12.705 --> 06:15.083
Hey, you little brat, don't be rude.

06:15.166 --> 06:16.542
Go play over there.

06:16.626 --> 06:19.587
-Ugh! You go play with the amateurs.
-[laughs]

06:19.670 --> 06:21.172
Come on, one more round.

06:21.255 --> 06:23.466
I'll beat you if we play another round.

06:24.884 --> 06:26.052
What's your name, boy?

06:27.345 --> 06:28.638
Chang-ho.

06:28.721 --> 06:29.597
Lee Chang-ho.

06:32.266 --> 06:33.559
Come here. Sit back down.

06:35.395 --> 06:38.981
Chang-ho. Good at life-and-death problems.

06:39.065 --> 06:43.069
LIFE-AND-DEATH: A PLAYER CAN SAVE
THEIR STONES OR KILL THE OPPONENT'S STONES

06:43.152 --> 06:43.986
[stones clattering]

06:46.155 --> 06:47.448
Find the black's lifeline.

06:47.532 --> 06:49.325
LIFELINE: A PATH
WHERE STONES CAN ESCAPE ALIVE

06:49.409 --> 06:51.160
This problem,
solve it and we'll play again.

06:51.244 --> 06:52.703
Are you sure about that?

06:53.413 --> 06:54.831
You have to keep your word.

06:55.581 --> 06:57.375
You know, you're not allowed
to take it back.

06:57.458 --> 06:58.584
[chuckles softly]

06:58.668 --> 07:00.920
[man] He's a Lee from Gyeongju too.

07:01.003 --> 07:02.922
A family elder kept talking about him,

07:03.005 --> 07:05.675
so I told him to bring the boy by.

07:06.384 --> 07:08.219
Well, he's good for a kid.

07:11.013 --> 07:13.516
That little kid has quite a temper,
doesn't he?

07:13.599 --> 07:16.602
-So he's your nephew?
-Nah, my first time seeing him too.

07:16.686 --> 07:20.815
The family tree's all messed up
so, he's actually a generation above.

07:20.898 --> 07:23.734
Looks like I'll be taking care
of a young uncle instead.

07:23.818 --> 07:25.361
[laughs]

07:25.445 --> 07:26.529
Your handicap?

07:28.614 --> 07:30.908
Wow. Played a pro
at only a disadvantage of four?

07:30.992 --> 07:33.870
THE NUMBER OF STONES THAT CORRESPONDS
TO A DIFFERENCE IN PLAYERS' STRENGTH

07:33.953 --> 07:36.205
Black? Not white?
Sure you didn't make a mistake?

07:36.289 --> 07:38.124
Mistake? Really?

07:38.708 --> 07:40.668
Why did you give him
an unsolvable problem?

07:40.751 --> 07:41.836
Just to confuse him, huh?

07:42.420 --> 07:44.046
Go problems don't have answers.

07:45.214 --> 07:46.883
I've never seen a play like his.

07:47.467 --> 07:50.428
His haengma and opening are all mixed-up…

07:50.511 --> 07:51.762
THE DIRECTION OR SHAPE OF STONES

07:51.846 --> 07:52.722
…but oddly powerful.

07:52.805 --> 07:54.640
OPENING TACTIC FOR THE GAME'S ADVANTAGE

07:55.266 --> 07:57.268
[clocks ticking]

08:03.107 --> 08:04.025
Ah.

08:06.986 --> 08:08.112
Is it solved?

08:08.196 --> 08:09.780
He can do this.

08:09.864 --> 08:13.075
-Bend and push. [laughs]
-No, no, no, right here.

08:13.159 --> 08:15.328
-There, I mean--
-Oh, come on.

08:15.411 --> 08:17.038
Ugh, what are you doing?

08:17.121 --> 08:20.416
I told you I had to really
concentrate a lot today.

08:20.917 --> 08:23.252
Stop staring at me,
or nothing will get done.

08:23.336 --> 08:25.087
Yes, I hear you.

08:25.171 --> 08:27.423
My grandson has important work,

08:27.507 --> 08:31.010
so let's step out and have a drink.
It'll be on me.

08:31.093 --> 08:32.678
-My treat, come on.
-I'm in trouble.

08:32.762 --> 08:35.389
If I drink during the day,
I know I'm going to pass out again.

08:35.473 --> 08:38.559
[old man] Yeah.
This guy can't even hold his milk--

08:38.643 --> 08:42.063
What about your homework?
You're concentrating on one thing?

08:42.146 --> 08:45.107
[clock striking]

08:45.191 --> 08:46.192
[sighs]

08:48.194 --> 08:49.779
[horns honking]

08:49.862 --> 08:53.241
[man] Third generation, only-son,
adored by his grandfather.

08:53.866 --> 08:57.495
Humor him and say the boy's good,
that he shows talent.

08:57.578 --> 08:59.455
I'll take care of all the rest.

09:02.458 --> 09:04.293
[man 1] Ah!

09:04.961 --> 09:10.174
Amazing, huh? His playing
has a lot of maturity! [laughs]

09:10.258 --> 09:12.218
-I'm number one at Go club…
-[man 1] Hah.

09:12.301 --> 09:15.555
[man 2] …but I'm lucky if I win one
out of ten matches with him.

09:15.638 --> 09:19.225
Everyone around him keeps filling him
with hot air, saying he's a prodigy,

09:20.184 --> 09:24.230
absorbed in this silly game
of stones instead of family business.

09:24.313 --> 09:27.692
[laughing] Go's stature
has been rising recently

09:27.775 --> 09:29.819
thanks to Champion Cho right here.

09:29.902 --> 09:32.029
There are more international competitions,

09:32.113 --> 09:35.241
so, you can enhance Korea's prestige too.

09:35.324 --> 09:37.076
[both laugh]

09:37.159 --> 09:39.453
-That's right.
-[laughs] Yes.

09:41.205 --> 09:42.290
That being said,

09:42.999 --> 09:44.292
Champion Cho,

09:44.375 --> 09:48.379
I was hoping that you could perhaps
take the boy on for a few months.

09:48.462 --> 09:50.506
I would compensate you handsomely,

09:50.590 --> 09:53.092
and sponsor you generously, of course.

09:54.051 --> 09:56.762
You really should use that money
to send him abroad

09:57.513 --> 09:59.140
for the family business.

09:59.223 --> 10:01.642
You can't improve at Go by studying hard.

10:03.603 --> 10:05.771
There's really no point
in me taking him on.

10:06.897 --> 10:07.732
Talent?

10:09.233 --> 10:10.151
Not a pinch.

10:10.818 --> 10:12.486
No matter how hard I look.

10:15.865 --> 10:16.782
Pro Cho!

10:17.491 --> 10:19.201
[exhales] Champion Cho!

10:20.328 --> 10:21.746
Hey, Cho Hoon-hyun!

10:23.914 --> 10:25.666
I worked for months trying to get that.

10:26.250 --> 10:29.045
Listen, man. You know
how much money he'll be sponsoring for us?

10:29.128 --> 10:30.713
What are we now, beggars?

10:31.213 --> 10:34.091
Business meetings, sponsorships,
they're all fine,

10:34.175 --> 10:36.093
but Go is more important than money.

10:37.011 --> 10:38.304
He said it was silly!

10:39.472 --> 10:40.431
Where's your pride?

10:41.349 --> 10:42.516
[man] Pride?

10:51.025 --> 10:53.527
[dog barking in distance]

11:00.117 --> 11:01.285
Min-je.

11:01.827 --> 11:04.038
Cho Min-je, what are you up to?

11:04.121 --> 11:05.414
-Daddy!
-Cho Min-je!

11:05.498 --> 11:07.249
-Yah! Whoo-hoo!
-[laughing]

11:07.333 --> 11:08.417
Ah, you're here!

11:08.501 --> 11:10.670
-[Min-je] I made this for you, Daddy!
-[Hoon-hyun laughs]

11:10.753 --> 11:13.964
Hey, Cho Min-je, I told you
not to touch the mail.

11:14.048 --> 11:15.424
-Leave it, leave it.
-[sighs]

11:15.508 --> 11:16.842
-I'll clean up.
-Come here.

11:16.926 --> 11:18.469
-Is the mail interesting? Huh?
-[grunts]

11:18.552 --> 11:21.389
Come on, let's go wash
your hands. Let's eat.

11:21.472 --> 11:24.684
-[Hoon-hyun sighs]
-Could you please turn on the stove?

11:24.767 --> 11:25.768
Let's go up.

11:25.851 --> 11:27.895
[Min-je] I want to eat sausage.

11:27.978 --> 11:29.980
[Hoon-hyun's wife]
You already had some this morning.

11:32.525 --> 11:33.859
[gentle music playing]

11:33.943 --> 11:35.903
KEEP YOUR PROMISE
FROM LEE CHANG-HO

11:35.986 --> 11:36.946
[chuckles softly]

11:38.114 --> 11:39.615
[phone ringing]

11:40.700 --> 11:42.702
Aw, man.

11:43.786 --> 11:44.662
Hello?

11:44.745 --> 11:46.706
Hey, Pro Lee. Cho Hoon-hyun.

11:46.789 --> 11:48.374
[Pro Lee on phone] Huh? Oh, right, yes.

11:48.958 --> 11:50.126
That boy, Chang-ho?

11:50.751 --> 11:52.294
Could I meet the boy again?

11:53.212 --> 11:54.088
LEE'S CLOCK SHOP

11:54.171 --> 11:56.674
-Oh, come on, let's go. Let's go.
-Hurry.

11:56.757 --> 11:59.593
SORRY, WE'RE CLOSED TODAY

12:01.387 --> 12:02.430
[stone clatters]

12:03.013 --> 12:04.598
Only three handicap stones.

12:05.266 --> 12:07.727
But if I win, you'll teach me Go.

12:08.436 --> 12:09.478
[inhales deeply]

12:09.562 --> 12:10.855
Why learn Go from me?

12:10.938 --> 12:13.023
I heard you're the strongest player.

12:13.691 --> 12:15.109
Korea's best player.

12:15.192 --> 12:16.277
[Pro Cheon] Hey, hey!

12:16.777 --> 12:20.781
Korea's best? He's the world's best.
You've got no idea kid.

12:21.407 --> 12:23.242
Hey. The masters are talking.

12:23.325 --> 12:25.870
-Stop interrupting us, novice.
-[laughs]

12:25.953 --> 12:28.414
You know, you're pretty rude
for a little kid.

12:28.497 --> 12:31.625
Last time, you little punk,
I gave four handicap stones.

12:31.709 --> 12:34.253
I'll knock you out
if we play an even game, you little brat!

12:34.336 --> 12:37.214
[scoffs] So you want to win
against a kid that badly, huh?

12:37.298 --> 12:38.924
[laughing]

12:41.051 --> 12:42.052
And what about…

12:43.512 --> 12:45.055
if you lose, what's my prize?

12:45.598 --> 12:47.600
[endearing music playing]

12:50.019 --> 12:50.936
BANANA MILK

12:51.020 --> 12:52.313
[Hoon-hyun chuckles]

12:53.481 --> 12:55.441
[inhales deeply] Okay.

12:55.983 --> 13:00.070
[chuckles] It's a done deal.
Cho Hoon-hyun came all the way here.

13:00.780 --> 13:02.364
[old man 1] What a smart son you have.

13:02.448 --> 13:03.491
-Hwa-chun!
-Huh?

13:03.574 --> 13:05.117
Don't just stand there, come here.

13:05.201 --> 13:06.410
-[laughs]
-Ay!

13:06.494 --> 13:08.454
[old man 2] He's really nervous.

13:08.537 --> 13:10.539
[gentle music playing]

13:10.623 --> 13:12.500
-[old men laughing]
-[Hwa-chun] Hmm.

13:13.375 --> 13:15.503
[dog barking]

13:16.837 --> 13:17.880
[stones clattering]

13:17.963 --> 13:19.298
[inhales deeply]

13:29.767 --> 13:32.019
It looks like I can't make
anymore moves here.

13:32.102 --> 13:34.230
It's over. I won, right?

13:34.939 --> 13:38.025
Yeah, I lost this time. You've improved.

13:40.569 --> 13:44.031
-[bell ringing]
-[laughing] Oh, you must be hungry.

13:44.114 --> 13:45.199
-Right?
-[old man chuckles]

13:45.282 --> 13:47.451
Oh, but who won?

13:47.535 --> 13:49.036
Mr. Chang-ho just won.

13:49.119 --> 13:52.289
-Oh wow, I can't believe it. [laughs]
-[stone clacking on board]

13:54.583 --> 13:56.919
Mr. Chang-ho, you're going to play again?

13:57.002 --> 14:00.172
It's one against one.
We're tied right now.

14:00.923 --> 14:02.633
So, do you like Go that much?

14:03.217 --> 14:06.512
It's awful.
When I lose, I can't sleep, I can't eat.

14:07.137 --> 14:08.973
It annoys me so much.

14:09.056 --> 14:11.976
But when I win,
there's nothing more fun in the world.

14:12.059 --> 14:13.102
[chuckles softly]

14:13.185 --> 14:14.895
Is that what keeps you playing, mister?

14:14.979 --> 14:17.314
-[men laugh]
-[old man] Oh, he's not a kid.

14:17.398 --> 14:19.358
[all laughing]

14:19.441 --> 14:21.735
-Let's, um…
-[stones clattering]

14:23.112 --> 14:24.321
…finish up in Seoul.

14:27.366 --> 14:28.951
-[grunts]
-[old man] Oh my.

14:31.120 --> 14:33.539
Calling me "mister…" Amateur.

14:33.622 --> 14:35.958
Oh, I don't mean you. [chuckles]

14:36.500 --> 14:37.543
[laughs]

14:38.210 --> 14:39.753
Call me "seonsaengnim."

14:39.837 --> 14:42.506
-[whimsical music plays]
-Seonsaengnim?

14:42.590 --> 14:43.716
-Goodness.
-Mm-hmm?

14:43.799 --> 14:46.010
-[old man 2] He's in. He is in!
-[old man 1 laughing]

14:46.093 --> 14:47.761
Chang-ho, what are you doing?

14:47.845 --> 14:50.723
Bow to your seonsaengnim.
To your new teacher.

14:50.806 --> 14:53.809
-Oh no, that's all right.
-[old man] What are you doing keeping him?

14:53.893 --> 14:56.270
-Let's say hurray.
-Hurray! [laughs]

14:56.353 --> 14:57.855
-Hurray for independence!
-Hurray!

14:57.938 --> 14:59.315
[sizzling]

15:00.733 --> 15:03.694
[Pro Cheon] You play three-day matches.
How are you gonna handle a student?

15:04.194 --> 15:06.405
You really think you can handle all that?

15:06.488 --> 15:08.866
[laughing] This is just between us,

15:08.949 --> 15:13.120
but you don't have the personality
to be a teacher, do you?

15:13.203 --> 15:14.830
[laughs]

15:17.249 --> 15:18.751
[sniffles]

15:20.002 --> 15:20.836
[slurping]

15:20.920 --> 15:23.047
Don't make more work for yourself, okay?

15:23.130 --> 15:24.340
Just focus on the match.

15:25.007 --> 15:27.885
What if you take him on as a student,
and he doesn't make it?

15:27.968 --> 15:30.220
So many people
already want to take you down.

15:30.304 --> 15:32.431
They'll go around saying
all sorts of crap.

15:32.514 --> 15:34.350
Wouldn't take him on
if going pro was the goal.

15:34.433 --> 15:35.809
[munching]

15:36.644 --> 15:38.103
[inhales deeply]

15:38.187 --> 15:41.565
I just got curious about
how he'd play when he's older.

15:42.191 --> 15:43.067
[slurping]

15:43.150 --> 15:45.986
[Hwa-chun] Chang-ho,
wear this at all times

15:46.070 --> 15:48.447
and think of this watch as me.

15:49.073 --> 15:50.449
Since you're doing this,

15:51.158 --> 15:53.202
give it your all so you won't regret it.

15:53.702 --> 15:56.664
Make sure to be studious and work hard.

15:57.539 --> 15:59.917
Make sure you listen to your seonsaengnim.

16:00.960 --> 16:02.044
Understand?

16:03.504 --> 16:04.546
Hmm.

16:05.422 --> 16:06.548
[engine powering]

16:06.632 --> 16:08.634
[motivational music playing]

16:13.389 --> 16:14.473
[train horn sounding]

16:27.194 --> 16:28.821
[doorbell ringing]

16:30.489 --> 16:32.866
-[banging on door]
-Champion Cho! Champion Cho!

16:32.950 --> 16:34.660
-Hey!
-[Hoon-hyun] You'll break the door.

16:34.743 --> 16:36.829
Hurry up! Hurry.

16:36.912 --> 16:39.456
Oh, gotta go! I gotta-- [groaning]

16:39.540 --> 16:40.916
What's with him?

16:41.000 --> 16:42.334
[Pro Lee whimpering]

16:43.460 --> 16:45.087
[Hoon-hyun] Right. Welcome.

16:45.170 --> 16:47.089
You must be tired. Come in.

16:52.803 --> 16:54.346
[toilet flushes]

16:54.430 --> 16:55.472
[door opens]

16:55.556 --> 16:56.432
[door closes]

16:56.515 --> 16:59.268
[Pro Lee] Oh,
I almost didn't make it. [laughs]

17:00.519 --> 17:04.064
Oh my gosh! Sure are a handsome boy.

17:04.148 --> 17:07.234
Wow, look at those strong bones
and wide shoulders.

17:07.776 --> 17:09.028
Your wish has come true.

17:09.111 --> 17:11.363
Perfect build
for wrestling, yeah! [laughs]

17:11.447 --> 17:12.614
[clears throat]

17:12.698 --> 17:15.117
-She's a girl.
-[Cho Min-je] "She's a girl."

17:15.701 --> 17:18.620
Oh, ma'am, I didn't mean, uh…
Congratulations to you both!

17:18.704 --> 17:21.123
-You've got two babies now! [laughs]
-[baby coos]

17:21.206 --> 17:23.000
[Hoon-hyun's wife]
You're right about that.

17:23.083 --> 17:24.960
-You're Chang-ho, right?
-Yeah.

17:25.544 --> 17:26.378
How do you do?

17:28.213 --> 17:30.382
-[chuckling]
-[baby cooing]

17:31.425 --> 17:33.010
This is the study.

17:34.386 --> 17:36.680
If you wanna read anything, go ahead.

17:41.727 --> 17:42.853
[exhales]

17:49.526 --> 17:51.028
I was about your age.

17:51.904 --> 17:53.405
Who's this older man?

17:54.656 --> 17:56.075
That's my seonsaengnim.

17:57.242 --> 17:58.327
[Chang-ho] Whoa.

17:58.869 --> 18:00.454
He looks so scary.

18:01.288 --> 18:04.792
-How old is he right now?
-He passed away a while ago.

18:05.542 --> 18:06.376
[clicks tongue]

18:06.460 --> 18:08.087
You're pretty lucky, huh?

18:08.754 --> 18:10.380
I'm not an old man quite yet.

18:12.174 --> 18:15.761
My grandpa said
that death doesn't care about your age.

18:16.428 --> 18:17.554
[sighs]

18:19.473 --> 18:20.474
Let's go eat.

18:22.059 --> 18:22.935
Come on.

18:26.063 --> 18:29.566
This liquor is Igangju,
but I don't feel drunk.

18:29.650 --> 18:31.693
-It deserves it's liquor of Joseon title.
-Yeah.

18:31.777 --> 18:35.614
Tell your grandpa
I appreciate it very much, okay?

18:35.697 --> 18:37.157
-Yes.
-How is the food?

18:37.241 --> 18:38.617
Does everything taste okay?

18:38.700 --> 18:40.160
Yes. It's delicious.

18:40.244 --> 18:42.204
You're a wonderful cook, madam.

18:42.704 --> 18:46.166
[chuckles] "Madam," um…
That doesn't sound right.

18:46.250 --> 18:47.501
[chuckles]

18:47.584 --> 18:49.586
Yeah. We're family now.

18:50.254 --> 18:51.255
That's a weird name.

18:52.047 --> 18:53.674
I have to call her something.

18:54.383 --> 18:57.219
-I'm not sure what to call her.
-He's right about that.

18:57.302 --> 18:58.887
Titles, once they get mixed up…

19:00.639 --> 19:01.473
are confusing.

19:01.557 --> 19:03.684
[laughing]

19:04.977 --> 19:06.103
What about "Auntie"?

19:06.895 --> 19:09.356
Just call me "Auntie"
from now on. That's nice.

19:11.900 --> 19:12.734
Okay.

19:14.820 --> 19:16.155
Want some more rice, Chang-ho?

19:16.947 --> 19:20.075
Yes. A little more please. Thanks, Auntie.

19:20.159 --> 19:21.410
[Hoon-hyun's wife chuckles]

19:21.952 --> 19:23.328
FUMIGATION

19:23.412 --> 19:26.415
[kids screaming, laughing]

19:38.385 --> 19:40.053
KOREA BADUK ASSOCIATION

19:40.137 --> 19:43.932
CONGRATULATIONS
CHO HOON-HYUN CONQUERS THE WORLD

19:44.641 --> 19:46.476
[curious music playing]

19:50.939 --> 19:52.024
Who are you?

19:52.107 --> 19:53.442
Looking for your dad?

19:53.525 --> 19:54.985
No, it's not that.

19:55.652 --> 19:57.988
I'm here to play some Go.

19:58.071 --> 19:59.239
Play Go?

19:59.323 --> 20:00.365
[stones clattering]

20:00.449 --> 20:02.451
[music continues]

20:10.125 --> 20:11.084
[boy 1] Who's that?

20:11.668 --> 20:13.754
[boy 2] I heard
he's Champion Cho's student.

20:14.254 --> 20:15.672
Anyone else?

20:17.966 --> 20:19.134
[boy 3] Where'd he come from?

20:19.218 --> 20:21.303
-[boy 4] Wow, he's amazing, seriously.
-[stone clacks]

20:21.386 --> 20:22.554
He's like a pro.

20:23.180 --> 20:25.432
[boy 5] Whoa, he's pushing it like that?

20:26.183 --> 20:27.643
[boy 6] I've never seen that before.

20:28.810 --> 20:30.145
[stones clattering]

20:31.605 --> 20:33.190
[boy 7] Whoa, what was that?

20:33.273 --> 20:35.317
Agh! Come on, really?

20:36.276 --> 20:39.238
There's so many.
I'll play everyone at once.

20:39.321 --> 20:41.365
-[chuckling]
-[boy 7] This kid is crazy.

20:41.448 --> 20:43.450
[orchestral music playing]

20:47.204 --> 20:49.498
[stones clinking]

20:54.419 --> 20:56.964
[boy 8] Wow, he really must be a prodigy.

20:57.756 --> 21:00.884
[boy 9] Champion Cho wouldn't have brought
him in from Jeonju if he wasn't.

21:00.968 --> 21:04.054
[boy 8] Yeah, Champion Cho found
a really good one.

21:04.137 --> 21:05.305
[stone clacks on board]

21:05.806 --> 21:07.557
-He's really good.
-He is.

21:07.641 --> 21:09.643
[music continues]

21:17.609 --> 21:19.653
-Ah!
-[stones clattering]

21:22.739 --> 21:24.783
[Chang-ho] There's a territory
here and here.

21:24.866 --> 21:27.202
And if you add the komi,
it's at least twenty.

21:28.161 --> 21:29.288
Want more?

21:29.371 --> 21:31.581
-[pensive music playing]
-[horns honking]

21:33.000 --> 21:34.960
HOSTED BY KOREA BADUK ASSOCIATION
SEJONG HOTEL

21:35.043 --> 21:37.170
THE NINTH GUKGI CHALLENGE MATCH
FOURTH ROUND

21:37.254 --> 21:39.548
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS NAM GI-CHEOL 8-DAN

21:42.092 --> 21:44.344
[woman] Mr. 9-dan Cho, 30 minutes left.

21:44.428 --> 21:46.346
CHALLENGE MATCH: FINAL MATCH

21:46.430 --> 21:48.724
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN, NAM GI-CHEOL 8-DAN

21:50.350 --> 21:53.353
[man] Champion Cho has a core of steel.
He's brutal.

21:53.437 --> 21:56.273
He won the match 30 minutes ago.
Why is he waiting?

21:56.356 --> 21:59.526
Expert Nam gets my respect
because, I mean,

21:59.609 --> 22:01.111
this has happened before,

22:01.194 --> 22:03.822
and he knows it'll get ugly
if he keeps going.

22:03.905 --> 22:05.949
Ah, I'm sick of this era of Cho and Nam.

22:06.658 --> 22:08.452
Nam Gi-cheol 8-dan,
this is your final byoyomi.

22:08.535 --> 22:10.996
BYOYOMI: TO ANNOUNCE
THE REMAINING TIME TO A PLAYER

22:11.079 --> 22:15.709
And one, two, three, four…

22:15.792 --> 22:16.835
-…five…
-[sighs]

22:17.753 --> 22:18.754
[woman] …six,

22:19.338 --> 22:21.340
seven, eight…

22:21.423 --> 22:23.008
-[stones clattering]
-[woman] …nine.

22:23.091 --> 22:25.135
[contemplative music playing]

22:25.218 --> 22:26.053
[stones clatter]

22:29.890 --> 22:31.433
I mean… [sighs]

22:32.976 --> 22:34.728
…should have blocked it there.

22:35.395 --> 22:37.564
[breathes deeply]

22:37.647 --> 22:38.774
What a wuss.

22:38.857 --> 22:40.442
[music continues]

22:44.404 --> 22:46.239
[exhales]

22:48.575 --> 22:49.910
[leg shaking]

22:52.287 --> 22:54.289
[exhales smoke]

22:56.208 --> 22:58.460
[Pro Lee] He's doing it. The Rattler.

22:58.543 --> 23:00.087
What's the Rattler?

23:00.170 --> 23:02.297
Hey, you don't know that? Huh?

23:02.381 --> 23:05.759
If Cho Hoon-hyun starts bouncing his leg,
that match is a sure win.

23:06.343 --> 23:09.721
It's like Sun Dong-yol stretching
in the bullpen in a game of baseball.

23:09.805 --> 23:10.722
[man] Oh.

23:10.806 --> 23:13.016
It makes the opponent
lose their concentration.

23:16.478 --> 23:17.312
[woman] One,

23:18.021 --> 23:18.855
two,

23:19.606 --> 23:20.440
three,

23:21.024 --> 23:21.900
four…

23:21.983 --> 23:25.654
[singing in Korean]
♪ The drizzle makes no sound ♪

23:26.279 --> 23:30.450
♪ We part at Busan station in sorrow ♪

23:32.119 --> 23:37.332
-♪ Goodbye, farewell ♪
-[rattling]

23:37.416 --> 23:40.085
♪ The train whistles as tears fall ♪

23:45.006 --> 23:47.217
[woman in English] A no-count win
by Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan.

23:47.300 --> 23:49.886
NO-COUNT WIN: A WIN SO DECISIVE
IT IS UNNECESSARY TO COUNT TERRITORIES

23:50.595 --> 23:53.056
Expert Nam seemed really angry today.

23:53.140 --> 23:57.060
Still, he should put back the stones.
Wow, what bad manners! Hmm.

23:57.144 --> 24:00.021
You, giving a lecture on manners?
"Parting at Busan"?

24:00.897 --> 24:04.192
You need to grind them into the ground,
to make it easier the next time.

24:04.276 --> 24:06.778
Don't worry. He'll be back
for revenge later. You'll see.

24:07.612 --> 24:11.825
Aigo! Congratulations!
Your song selection was great today.

24:11.908 --> 24:14.953
I already see the headlines
that'll be up tomorrow.

24:15.036 --> 24:18.790
Ah, Mr. Chang-ho is going through
Gwancheol-dong as we speak.

24:18.874 --> 24:22.043
He's mowing through all the apprentices
like they're grass. [laughs]

24:22.127 --> 24:24.045
Word has spread everywhere

24:24.129 --> 24:26.673
that the tiger cub you brought back
is a total prodigy.

24:26.756 --> 24:28.133
-[laughs]
-Yeah, but…

24:28.216 --> 24:31.595
Hey, don't mention that prodigy stuff
around him. Just don't do it.

24:32.471 --> 24:33.722
It won't do him any good.

24:36.850 --> 24:37.976
[Hoon-hyun] Wait for me.

24:39.269 --> 24:40.479
Seonsaengnim.

24:41.897 --> 24:44.441
-What's this?
-[chuckles] Candy.

24:45.525 --> 24:46.610
We're here, Auntie.

24:46.693 --> 24:47.861
Oh. You're together?

24:48.987 --> 24:50.405
We ran into each other.

24:50.489 --> 24:52.991
-You did well, Chang-ho?
-Yes. Thanks, Auntie.

24:53.074 --> 24:54.284
How was the match today?

24:55.410 --> 24:56.495
-I lost.
-Hmm.

24:57.537 --> 24:59.080
You always say you lost.

25:02.209 --> 25:03.168
[exhales sharply]

25:03.793 --> 25:06.796
The opening, haengma, reading,
they're all terrible.

25:06.880 --> 25:08.882
READING: TO THINK IN ADVANCE
WHERE TO PLACE A STONE

25:08.965 --> 25:10.800
But do you know what's worst among those?

25:10.884 --> 25:12.636
It is your terrible attitude.

25:12.719 --> 25:13.720
Huh?

25:14.554 --> 25:16.264
I won against everyone.

25:16.348 --> 25:18.934
The older players
weren't anything special.

25:19.017 --> 25:20.519
[Hoon-hyun] Winning isn't everything.

25:21.520 --> 25:26.149
You've only studied Go a few months.
These guys have been studying for years.

25:26.816 --> 25:29.152
Your moves got lazy
since you were at an advantage.

25:29.236 --> 25:33.782
It's good manners to always do your best.
And learn to respect your opponent first.

25:33.865 --> 25:35.617
But you shake your leg.

25:36.326 --> 25:38.328
You do. And you hum.

25:38.411 --> 25:39.246
You…

25:40.372 --> 25:41.790
Hey… [exhales sharply]

25:42.707 --> 25:43.542
[grunts]

25:44.084 --> 25:45.126
Hey, punk…

25:47.462 --> 25:49.548
save that for when you're the best.

25:51.174 --> 25:52.425
[scoffs, sniffles]

25:52.509 --> 25:53.635
Let's, uh…

25:56.263 --> 25:58.056
We'll start with the basics.

25:58.807 --> 26:00.100
But I read that book.

26:00.642 --> 26:03.228
Basics are boring, and they're easy.

26:03.311 --> 26:04.354
Easy?

26:07.065 --> 26:10.819
-Black or white, what's better?
-White has the advantage. It's obvious.

26:16.408 --> 26:17.284
Take white.

26:18.159 --> 26:19.619
[gentle music playing]

26:25.083 --> 26:27.794
Good moves don't come
from thinking for a long time.

26:27.877 --> 26:29.462
Thinking is what bad players do.

26:30.255 --> 26:32.173
It's time to cultivate game sense.

26:33.174 --> 26:34.926
That doesn't mean play impulsively.

26:37.137 --> 26:38.471
Don't back down.

26:39.055 --> 26:41.224
The essence of Go is
the battle, the attack.

26:44.519 --> 26:45.937
Still think white's better?

26:48.064 --> 26:49.065
I don't.

26:50.066 --> 26:51.026
Take black.

26:53.945 --> 26:55.905
[stones clacking]

27:04.080 --> 27:05.707
[stones clattering]

27:05.790 --> 27:09.002
I played only using the basics.
Tell me why you're losing.

27:09.502 --> 27:11.379
[music continues]

27:13.506 --> 27:16.468
"Genius," "prodigy," don't believe
when people mention that.

27:17.010 --> 27:19.179
You're good at calculations
and memorizing.

27:19.679 --> 27:21.598
You're only imitating how to play Go.

27:23.475 --> 27:25.268
Don't be cocky. Learn the basics.

27:27.520 --> 27:28.355
[grunts]

27:29.564 --> 27:32.359
Use your right hand when playing,
if nothing else.

27:32.442 --> 27:34.903
It is basic courtesy
when playing your opponent.

27:36.279 --> 27:37.113
Okay.

27:39.449 --> 27:40.992
[Hoon-hyun] Stamina is everything.

27:41.910 --> 27:43.953
The rashness of an impulsive move.

27:44.788 --> 27:47.415
The complacency of wanting to compromise.

27:48.208 --> 27:50.335
The arrogance of wanting
to finish quickly.

27:50.877 --> 27:53.505
These things happen
when your stamina fails,

27:53.588 --> 27:55.757
and they'll lead to your defeat.

27:57.008 --> 27:57.967
[panting]

27:58.051 --> 28:00.053
[music continues]

28:04.349 --> 28:05.183
[hisses]

28:07.686 --> 28:10.146
Ah, no. I'll use my right hand.

28:13.358 --> 28:15.276
[music continues]

28:21.908 --> 28:24.119
DEAR GRANDPA
I HOPE YOU'RE WELL

28:24.202 --> 28:26.204
[music continues]

28:30.583 --> 28:32.961
[stones clattering]

28:34.504 --> 28:36.506
[music continues]

29:10.790 --> 29:12.000
[stone clacks on board]

29:14.711 --> 29:15.962
[music fades]

29:16.045 --> 29:18.423
ONE STEP, ONE MOVE

29:18.506 --> 29:19.716
[deliver man] Ugh…

29:21.968 --> 29:25.346
Who eats Chinese food on the rooftop?
Are you kidding me?

29:44.949 --> 29:45.867
[door closes]

29:49.245 --> 29:50.747
[slurping]

30:00.256 --> 30:02.258
[slurping]

30:04.469 --> 30:05.303
Hello.

30:05.386 --> 30:06.846
Do you always come up here?

30:09.849 --> 30:11.976
Man! Couldn't they have ordered together?

30:12.936 --> 30:15.855
What's their problem?
Why can't they eat at the restaurant?

30:16.940 --> 30:18.900
[slurping]

30:18.983 --> 30:21.861
Champion Cho must be working like crazy
to keep you fed.

30:24.322 --> 30:25.198
Do you…

30:26.950 --> 30:28.326
know who I am?

30:28.910 --> 30:30.662
Yeah, of course I know who you are.

30:31.746 --> 30:34.833
You're the pro Nam Gi-cheol,
my seonsaengnim's rival.

30:35.917 --> 30:36.960
Rival? Please.

30:37.043 --> 30:38.294
[Chang-ho slurping]

30:38.378 --> 30:39.838
"KING OF GO" EXPANDS HIS FOOTPRINT!

30:39.921 --> 30:42.340
Don't relax now that you're a pro.
Keep studying.

30:42.423 --> 30:44.217
Your teacher is extremely good.

30:44.300 --> 30:45.260
Well,

30:46.928 --> 30:47.804
you see,

30:49.889 --> 30:52.851
I'm not sure if it's something
I can learn just by studying.

30:54.519 --> 30:57.230
I would love to be just half
as good as his pinky toe,

30:59.023 --> 31:01.109
but I just don't seem to have the talent.

31:03.528 --> 31:05.655
[tsks] Don't just try to learn.

31:06.281 --> 31:07.490
You should try to win.

31:08.074 --> 31:09.284
[hopeful music playing]

31:09.367 --> 31:11.327
Then you'll naturally learn.

31:12.161 --> 31:13.997
That's what I did when I played him.

31:15.081 --> 31:16.499
[slurping]

31:19.502 --> 31:22.881
CHO HOON-HYUN'S LEGENDARY MATCHES

31:22.964 --> 31:24.799
WHITE CHO HOON-HYUN
BLACK KIM SEONG-JU

31:24.883 --> 31:26.885
[hopeful music continues]

31:31.306 --> 31:32.473
[sighs]

31:32.557 --> 31:34.559
Wow, it moves so quickly.

31:35.518 --> 31:37.228
How do I capture this?

31:38.187 --> 31:40.440
Maybe going head-on won't help at all.

31:41.524 --> 31:43.234
Should I just hold?

31:43.318 --> 31:45.320
[music continues]

31:46.863 --> 31:48.197
[sighs]

31:55.330 --> 31:58.082
[stones clattering]

32:01.878 --> 32:04.839
Chang-ho is working late tonight.

32:05.381 --> 32:06.382
[Hoon-hyun] Mm-hmm.

32:07.342 --> 32:08.968
So, how's it going?

32:10.136 --> 32:11.888
Preliminaries are coming up, right?

32:12.513 --> 32:14.807
How he does right now isn't important.

32:16.059 --> 32:17.685
It's about finding his own Go.

32:19.062 --> 32:21.272
You know, rushing him
won't do him any good.

32:21.898 --> 32:24.817
Don't just push him,
coax and soothe him, honey.

32:24.901 --> 32:25.902
Chang-ho's still a kid.

32:26.527 --> 32:28.780
He'll be spoiled if I baby him like a kid.

32:30.531 --> 32:31.824
I made him come to Seoul.

32:32.700 --> 32:35.828
I can't slack off in teaching him.
I need to make him the best.

32:37.038 --> 32:40.041
Competition life is too sad if

32:41.459 --> 32:42.877
you're not top dog.

32:44.045 --> 32:47.006
THE 7TH DAEWANG TOURNAMENT
FIRST PRELIMINARY ROUND

32:47.090 --> 32:49.092
[gentle music playing]

32:51.678 --> 32:53.680
[stones clattering]

33:07.402 --> 33:09.404
[ticking]

33:10.238 --> 33:12.240
[ticking echoes]

33:16.661 --> 33:18.663
[ticking slows down]

33:20.373 --> 33:21.916
[laughing]

33:23.042 --> 33:26.879
I mean, he keeps staring at the board
like it'll magically move or something.

33:27.505 --> 33:30.842
You know, I thought
he was falling asleep during the match.

33:30.925 --> 33:32.176
-[laughs]
-[sighs]

33:32.260 --> 33:35.263
You know, the kid plays Go
like he's pushing 60 years old.

33:36.222 --> 33:38.641
-He's lost two rounds in a row.
-Aish!

33:38.725 --> 33:41.811
-Hey, Pro Noh, how much did you lose?
-A couple hundred.

33:41.894 --> 33:42.729
Hmm.

33:42.812 --> 33:44.897
I'm losing all my earnings
on bets like this.

33:45.857 --> 33:48.693
I heard he was Cho's student,
so I thought he'd be winning more.

33:48.776 --> 33:52.655
I mean, he used to be a bright kid,
so why's he been getting worse?

33:52.739 --> 33:54.949
And his personality
is getting weirder too.

33:55.033 --> 33:58.745
[man] Champion Cho probably hounds him
all day and night with that temper of his.

33:58.828 --> 34:02.123
And he's living with him too,
so it makes sense.

34:05.334 --> 34:06.294
[Chang-ho] Grandpa…

34:07.170 --> 34:10.131
Seonsaengnim Cho's Go
is flashy and strong,

34:10.214 --> 34:11.674
but it doesn't suit me.

34:12.175 --> 34:14.052
I'm going to find my own Go,

34:14.677 --> 34:19.140
something no one else can replicate,
even if it takes time.

34:21.017 --> 34:22.685
[Hoon-hyun] That's not it!

34:22.769 --> 34:25.980
The geima at the top right corner,
attach, push at the top edge, extending.

34:26.064 --> 34:27.523
Where is everything I've taught you?

34:27.607 --> 34:28.691
Honey.

34:29.484 --> 34:31.152
-It's getting late.
-Leave us.

34:31.235 --> 34:32.945
You can't win all the time.

34:33.029 --> 34:35.573
He's already upset
about the loss, you know.

34:35.656 --> 34:37.241
Stay out of it, please.

34:37.784 --> 34:39.035
[crickets chirping]

34:42.288 --> 34:45.500
You hold when you should push
and push when you should hold.

34:46.167 --> 34:47.251
Why are you offbeat?

34:47.335 --> 34:48.461
[inhales deeply]

34:49.045 --> 34:52.215
I thought the variables
would increase with a fight,

34:52.298 --> 34:54.050
so it'd be better to wait until--

34:54.133 --> 34:55.176
I told you.

34:56.094 --> 34:58.971
Go isn't about compromising
and building territories.

34:59.555 --> 35:01.474
Instead, you need to bite,
scratch, and claw!

35:03.559 --> 35:06.062
That's not my style, seonsaengnim.
That is what you would do.

35:06.145 --> 35:07.271
Don't give me lip--

35:07.355 --> 35:08.439
Style?

35:09.357 --> 35:10.399
Play style?

35:10.983 --> 35:12.819
Lose and none of that stuff matters!

35:13.319 --> 35:15.446
Learn to play! Follow the pattern.

35:16.114 --> 35:19.617
[inhales] Does everyone in the world need
to play Go the same as you?

35:19.700 --> 35:21.786
All I'm saying is there's an order!

35:22.745 --> 35:25.957
You need to have a reason
for every stone you put down.

35:26.040 --> 35:27.917
A reason behind every retreat.

35:28.751 --> 35:32.672
You can't make your own style
or anything without the basics!

35:33.798 --> 35:34.799
[sighs]

35:38.553 --> 35:40.429
[sighs] It's the same here.

35:41.430 --> 35:45.726
It's only natural to extend over here,
so why would you retreat? Why?

35:46.936 --> 35:48.146
Why are you so defiant?

35:51.357 --> 35:54.986
I know that might be what's right,
but there is a…

35:56.320 --> 35:58.114
small chance tables turn.

35:58.781 --> 36:02.160
And if I make this move,

36:02.243 --> 36:03.744
I'm one hundred percent sure

36:05.580 --> 36:07.290
that I'll keep half a point.

36:08.124 --> 36:09.125
A hundred percent?

36:09.917 --> 36:12.336
Chang-ho, how many times did I tell you

36:13.087 --> 36:16.340
staking out territories in the center
becomes too much of a risk!

36:16.424 --> 36:18.551
I'm sure that you're right, but…

36:19.093 --> 36:20.428
[inhales deeply]

36:21.012 --> 36:23.681
…I thought I could do
the calculations, so…

36:23.764 --> 36:24.807
[stones clattering]

36:25.516 --> 36:27.226
…uh, I experimented here.

36:29.312 --> 36:30.479
Experimented?

36:33.399 --> 36:35.067
You think Go is a piece of cake.

36:36.444 --> 36:39.739
You disregard the basics,
use petty tricks instead,

36:39.822 --> 36:41.949
and stubbornly cling to your own ideas.

36:42.033 --> 36:42.992
[sighs]

36:46.037 --> 36:46.871
Let's stop.

36:48.080 --> 36:51.250
There's no point in getting angry
when you don't want to learn.

36:57.048 --> 36:58.424
[door closes]

36:59.050 --> 37:00.927
[somber music playing]

37:04.847 --> 37:07.934
[Chang-ho] And if I make this move,

37:08.017 --> 37:09.769
I'm one hundred percent sure

37:11.520 --> 37:13.356
that I'll keep half a point.

37:16.776 --> 37:19.695
[Hoon-hyun] Those who play first,
have the advantage in Go.

37:20.279 --> 37:22.198
When players of the same rank play,

37:22.740 --> 37:25.701
the first player is disadvantaged
five and a half points.

37:26.869 --> 37:28.079
That's called komi.

37:28.162 --> 37:29.205
[sighs]

37:29.288 --> 37:31.332
[uplifting music playing]

37:31.415 --> 37:34.168
The half a point here is to prevent a tie,

37:34.877 --> 37:37.296
and such a thing
does not actually exist on the board.

37:40.675 --> 37:43.469
It's the minimum unit deciding a match

37:43.552 --> 37:45.888
and does not visibly exist on the board.

37:47.431 --> 37:49.350
Perhaps, this kid
is seeing something else here.

37:49.433 --> 37:51.644
BLACK WINS BY 1.5 POINTS

37:51.727 --> 37:54.563
[music continues]

38:05.741 --> 38:07.660
RESPECTFULLY YOURS, CHANG-HO

38:12.665 --> 38:15.668
SIR, AUNTIE, THANK YOU FOR EVERYTHING
SORRY TO DISAPPOINT YOU

38:17.628 --> 38:18.754
[sighs]

38:22.842 --> 38:23.718
[woman] Yes, where to?

38:25.136 --> 38:27.054
9:40 bus to Jeonju, please.

38:27.138 --> 38:28.764
[man] All right, 9:40 bus to Jeonju!

38:28.848 --> 38:30.057
SEOUL - JEONJU

38:30.141 --> 38:32.059
The 9:40 bus is now leaving!

38:33.060 --> 38:35.396
Okay, okay, anyone else boarding?

38:36.480 --> 38:38.441
Okay, we have everyone, right?

38:49.076 --> 38:50.328
Aigo!

38:51.037 --> 38:52.955
-Seonsaengnim.
-[Hoon-hyun grunts softly]

38:54.915 --> 38:55.791
[grunts]

38:58.377 --> 38:59.337
[grunts]

39:02.006 --> 39:04.008
[slurping]

39:08.721 --> 39:09.680
Yesterday,

39:11.432 --> 39:14.560
the half point you talked about,

39:15.686 --> 39:18.939
it turns out you weren't completely wrong.

39:19.482 --> 39:21.317
It doesn't make it right, though.

39:21.817 --> 39:22.693
I just

39:24.236 --> 39:25.863
haven't found the right move yet.

39:32.745 --> 39:34.538
Go doesn't have answers,

39:36.499 --> 39:38.417
but I was forcing you to give me one.

39:40.669 --> 39:41.545
I'm sorry.

39:42.838 --> 39:44.173
Better to walk steady

39:45.049 --> 39:46.759
than try to run and wobble.

39:48.552 --> 39:50.638
You found your Go. That's good enough.

39:54.141 --> 39:55.935
If that's the decision you've made,

39:56.435 --> 39:57.728
take responsibility.

39:58.687 --> 39:59.688
In both Go

40:00.689 --> 40:01.565
and in life.

40:05.236 --> 40:06.278
Understand?

40:06.362 --> 40:08.364
[breathing emotionally]

40:09.198 --> 40:11.242
[hopeful music playing]

40:15.538 --> 40:17.748
Your fighting spirit is eighty percent.

40:18.999 --> 40:21.460
Even if you lose,
you can't let them take you in spirit.

40:22.420 --> 40:23.587
It's better to hide it.

40:24.130 --> 40:27.758
Your thoughts, emotions, your breathing.

40:28.968 --> 40:31.137
Do not show vulnerability
to your opponent.

40:32.012 --> 40:35.307
I know, but, um, it's not easy to do.

40:35.391 --> 40:38.811
[exhales] Think about something
familiar and comfortable.

40:38.894 --> 40:40.146
[inhales deeply]

40:40.229 --> 40:43.232
Something that just relaxes you
by thinking of it.

40:44.859 --> 40:47.653
The match is over
the moment you lose your composure.

40:48.487 --> 40:49.488
[sighs]

40:50.489 --> 40:51.824
[music continues]

40:53.576 --> 40:55.744
Don't view the stones by color.

40:57.538 --> 40:59.582
Every move needs a reason behind it.

41:00.249 --> 41:01.459
Territories

41:02.626 --> 41:06.088
come into form naturally
and cannot be built with force.

41:07.131 --> 41:09.133
Take care of each and every stone.

41:10.384 --> 41:11.343
At some point,

41:11.886 --> 41:14.889
the stones will have moved
towards harmony.

41:14.972 --> 41:16.265
[stones clattering]

41:17.683 --> 41:22.480
29TH CHOEGOWI FINAL PRELIMINARY

41:23.814 --> 41:25.149
[sighs]

41:26.108 --> 41:27.860
[Pro Cheon] Champion Cho,
aren't you going up?

41:27.943 --> 41:29.028
Don't have to.

41:29.695 --> 41:34.366
Aigo. Mr. Chang-ho just had to end up
with Pro Ko again, the old-timer.

41:34.450 --> 41:37.036
-[stones clattering]
-[Hoon-hyun] Hey, don't worry about him.

41:37.119 --> 41:40.414
[chuckles softly] You should be
figuring out how to survive Chang-ho.

41:40.998 --> 41:42.208
He's an odd one.

41:42.708 --> 41:48.130
Doesn't even review his games properly,
but he somehow keeps getting better.

41:48.214 --> 41:49.131
[exhales]

41:49.215 --> 41:52.676
His opening is sloppy
and his haengma is slow,

41:53.427 --> 41:55.346
but he somehow builds a position.

41:55.971 --> 41:59.308
His calculations
might be better than mine.

41:59.808 --> 42:02.811
So does he still play
like he's a 60-year-old grandfather?

42:02.895 --> 42:03.896
No.

42:04.897 --> 42:05.898
Like he's 80.

42:06.524 --> 42:09.151
[all laugh]

42:09.235 --> 42:11.237
[uplifting music playing]

42:15.324 --> 42:18.035
[Chang-ho] I'm going to protect
half a point for certainty

42:18.118 --> 42:20.788
rather than make a whole point
through a fight.

42:21.580 --> 42:25.042
In the end, Go is a fight for territories.

42:25.543 --> 42:26.794
[sighs]

42:26.877 --> 42:30.714
Grandpa, I think
I've finally found my own Go.

42:31.382 --> 42:32.883
It's a bit rough,

42:32.967 --> 42:35.761
and it's not flashy
like Seonsaengnim Cho's,

42:36.512 --> 42:40.808
but it's going to be impossible
for anyone to beat.

42:40.891 --> 42:42.393
[music crescendoes]

42:42.476 --> 42:43.352
[music ends]

42:43.435 --> 42:44.436
[sizzling]

42:45.104 --> 42:46.021
[Pro Cheon chortles]

42:46.105 --> 42:48.274
-[man] That's good.
-Yeah, that's a good piece.

42:48.357 --> 42:49.900
[chuckles]

42:49.984 --> 42:51.443
[exclaims, chuckles]

42:52.695 --> 42:56.073
The energy must be excellent
here at Yeonhui-dong, right?

42:56.657 --> 42:59.326
Two soaring professional players
under the same roof.

42:59.410 --> 43:00.244
[grunts]

43:00.744 --> 43:02.913
Chang-ho, sir, congratulations!

43:02.997 --> 43:05.916
You're making good time,
already heading to finals!

43:06.000 --> 43:09.336
Shouldn't we take a photograph
to remember this?

43:10.421 --> 43:13.465
Pro Cheon, could you take
a family photo for us?

43:13.549 --> 43:15.426
[laughing] Yeah.

43:22.266 --> 43:23.267
Now…

43:23.350 --> 43:24.768
One, two!

43:26.270 --> 43:27.730
Chang-ho, come on, kid, smile.

43:27.813 --> 43:29.064
Why do you look so sad?

43:29.982 --> 43:31.734
What? He's smiling really big.

43:32.359 --> 43:33.444
Yeah, he's smiling.

43:34.361 --> 43:35.821
-Oh, really?
-Yes.

43:36.864 --> 43:38.866
O-Okay, then, here we go. Ready?

43:39.491 --> 43:42.453
-One, two, three!
-[camera clicks]

43:47.416 --> 43:48.626
But I think

43:49.501 --> 43:52.087
it'd be better for the white
to bend this way here.

43:52.713 --> 43:54.715
That could be a good move, but…

43:55.924 --> 43:57.968
I'm thinking it could leave an opening.

43:58.052 --> 43:59.970
Still, it'd be simple to cut off.

44:03.599 --> 44:05.100
You're not even leaping there,

44:05.184 --> 44:07.144
you'd rather take the long way around.

44:08.604 --> 44:09.938
I don't love it, but…

44:10.022 --> 44:14.193
[inhales deeply] …well, no one
will be judging me for it, either.

44:16.028 --> 44:17.029
Who are you playing?

44:17.529 --> 44:19.406
I'm playing Pro Nam Gi-cheol.

44:20.199 --> 44:21.408
[chuckles softly]

44:21.492 --> 44:24.036
I'm, uh… I'm worried about it.

44:24.119 --> 44:26.789
I mean, his Go is fierce,
but you know this, of course.

44:27.414 --> 44:28.707
He's persistent.

44:30.084 --> 44:33.587
If you start to back down, he'll think
you're weak and start attacking.

44:34.213 --> 44:35.798
You need to come at him strong.

44:36.548 --> 44:38.300
I'm going to start in defense mode.

44:38.384 --> 44:39.802
[sucks teeth] You little punk!

44:40.511 --> 44:41.595
[chuckles softly]

44:41.679 --> 44:43.806
You told me I should find my own Go.

44:43.889 --> 44:45.224
Should I stand back?

44:47.017 --> 44:48.268
Believe in me.

44:49.520 --> 44:50.437
Okay.

44:51.480 --> 44:53.440
Think of it as a lesson. Don't be nervous.

44:54.608 --> 44:55.442
Okay.

44:58.195 --> 44:59.154
I'm going…

45:00.280 --> 45:01.740
I'm going to beat him.

45:03.867 --> 45:09.373
23RD WANGWI COMPETITION FINALS
12TH ROUND

45:09.456 --> 45:11.458
[pensive music playing]

45:14.670 --> 45:16.296
[stones clattering]

45:22.761 --> 45:24.138
[man] Nam 9-dan, black.

45:24.722 --> 45:26.223
Lee 3-dan, white.

45:28.267 --> 45:29.435
Let the match begin.

45:29.518 --> 45:31.770
29TH CHOEGOWI MATCH
CHALLENGER SELECTION

45:31.854 --> 45:34.148
NAM GI-CHEOL 9-DAN VS LEE CHANG-HO 3-DAN

45:35.774 --> 45:37.067
[stones clattering]

45:38.569 --> 45:40.154
[stones clattering]

45:47.453 --> 45:48.370
Mr. Lee.

45:48.454 --> 45:49.788
-[gasps] Oh! My goodness.
-[laughs]

45:49.872 --> 45:52.166
Why don't we go to the review room,
have some fresh coffee?

45:52.249 --> 45:55.169
Ah, no. I won't understand
anything anyway.

45:55.252 --> 45:56.670
-It's all right.
-Ah. [chuckles]

45:56.754 --> 45:58.213
[music continues]

46:01.550 --> 46:03.010
[stones clattering]

46:03.719 --> 46:04.803
[stone clacks on board]

46:06.096 --> 46:08.098
[stones clattering]

46:09.767 --> 46:10.684
[stone clacks on board]

46:20.652 --> 46:22.446
[stones clattering]

46:29.411 --> 46:30.746
[inhales deeply]

46:30.829 --> 46:33.165
[exhales smoke]

46:36.877 --> 46:38.462
[stones clattering]

46:38.545 --> 46:41.423
Cho 9-dan, ten minutes left.

46:42.424 --> 46:43.759
Oh, uh… uh…

46:44.343 --> 46:45.469
Okay…

46:52.851 --> 46:54.812
I… Well, uh…

46:55.354 --> 46:58.565
[woman] No-count win for white,
Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan.

47:01.568 --> 47:02.736
Oh, Pro Baek.

47:03.779 --> 47:05.030
Thank you for the lesson.

47:07.866 --> 47:10.035
-Hey, Champion Cho.
-[Pro Lee clears throat]

47:10.619 --> 47:12.496
The black seems to be at an advantage.

47:12.579 --> 47:14.706
Oh, and what would you know about that?

47:14.790 --> 47:16.333
Didn't you get crushed too?

47:16.416 --> 47:19.294
I didn't get crushed, you punk.
I was drunk that day.

47:19.378 --> 47:21.505
Here's the record to the 115th move.

47:23.090 --> 47:24.258
Mm-hmm.

47:25.259 --> 47:26.468
[sighs]

47:29.972 --> 47:31.223
[chuckles softly]

47:38.897 --> 47:41.567
[sucks teeth]
Shouldn't have cut that. Hmm.

47:42.776 --> 47:44.570
If I took it…

47:49.241 --> 47:52.703
[Chang-ho] Push one
and expand to the center.

47:55.956 --> 47:57.040
[Gi-cheol inhales deeply]

47:57.124 --> 47:58.625
[grunts, exhales]

48:00.419 --> 48:02.129
[clicks tongues, inhales sharply]

48:02.212 --> 48:04.798
A game between you and Champion Cho
will be worth watching.

48:05.716 --> 48:06.592
Hmm?

48:08.844 --> 48:11.096
You're better than your teacher
in closing.

48:12.139 --> 48:13.056
Congratulations.

48:17.853 --> 48:18.854
[clears throat]

48:19.980 --> 48:21.607
Expert Nam collapsed at the end.

48:21.690 --> 48:24.735
See, man? Chang-ho's just strong.
I'm not weak. [chuckles]

48:24.818 --> 48:26.862
[Pro Lee] Something about that energy
in Yeonhui-dong.

48:26.945 --> 48:28.030
29TH CHOEGOWI TOURNAMENT

48:30.365 --> 48:32.492
LEE CHANG-HO

48:32.576 --> 48:33.410
CHALLENGER

48:33.493 --> 48:34.912
[chuckles]

48:36.580 --> 48:38.582
[pensive music playing]

48:42.169 --> 48:43.712
[laughs] Oh my.

48:44.254 --> 48:46.590
I cannot believe
that this match has come so quickly.

48:46.673 --> 48:48.675
CHOEGOWI FINAL
LEE CHANG-HO VS CHO HOON-HYUN

48:48.759 --> 48:50.677
He won his way up. What can I say?

48:52.346 --> 48:53.972
What happens if Chang-ho
actually beats ya?

48:54.056 --> 48:55.682
Oh yeah? Please.

48:56.224 --> 48:57.893
In ten years, maybe.

48:57.976 --> 49:00.020
[train brakes squealing]

49:00.103 --> 49:03.106
[announcer over PA] Please watch your step
while exiting the train.

49:06.234 --> 49:07.069
Doors closing.

49:07.152 --> 49:08.737
[train door hissing close]

49:13.617 --> 49:15.994
WINS THE YING SHIBEI CUP!
UNIFIES THE WORLD!

49:23.919 --> 49:26.380
[gentle music playing]

49:50.153 --> 49:51.655
CHO HOON-HYUN VS SEO GEON-WOO

49:57.536 --> 49:59.496
[Chang-ho] Seonsaengnim's haengma is weak

50:00.205 --> 50:01.957
when he's been attacked in a game.

50:04.960 --> 50:09.589
When the framework expands,
his check is always weak.

50:11.508 --> 50:12.718
[sighs]

50:16.513 --> 50:18.056
Seonsaengnim, dinner's ready.

50:18.140 --> 50:19.141
-[book thuds]
-Yeah.

50:22.561 --> 50:24.271
Ah, here's the book.

50:38.618 --> 50:42.414
[exhales sharply] Hey, uh, honey, come on,
you should talk to him.

50:42.497 --> 50:44.124
You're his seonsaengnim, right?

50:44.833 --> 50:46.001
What do you want me to…

50:46.835 --> 50:49.588
Did you sleep well? Are you okay?

50:50.213 --> 50:51.256
I'm good, Auntie.

50:53.008 --> 50:54.551
Don't get hung up on winning.

50:56.887 --> 50:58.430
Just play your own way.

51:01.308 --> 51:02.142
Yes.

51:03.226 --> 51:04.269
CHALLENGE MATCH
LAST ROUND

51:04.352 --> 51:05.520
-Is that the car?
-Yes, it is.

51:05.604 --> 51:07.814
FEBRUARY 2ND 1990
KOREA BADUK ASSOCIATION, GWANCHEOL-DONG

51:07.898 --> 51:09.524
-They came in the same car.
-Get a photo!

51:09.608 --> 51:12.861
[reporter 1] Champion Cho, will you open
aggressively today as well?

51:12.944 --> 51:14.863
Will you go easy on your student?

51:14.946 --> 51:17.282
-[reporters clamoring]
-[sighs] Wait, wait.

51:19.534 --> 51:20.452
[exhales]

51:20.535 --> 51:21.411
[grunts]

51:21.953 --> 51:22.788
You'll do well.

51:23.663 --> 51:24.498
Thanks.

51:25.207 --> 51:27.209
[anticipatory music playing]

51:42.182 --> 51:44.184
[cameras clicking]

51:44.267 --> 51:45.560
[music continues]

52:07.666 --> 52:09.292
Choose your stones, please.

52:24.099 --> 52:27.811
Lee 4-dan, black. Cho 9-dan, white.

52:30.564 --> 52:31.898
Let the game begin.

52:31.982 --> 52:33.692
29TH CHOEGOWI CHALLENGE MATCH
LAST ROUND

52:33.775 --> 52:37.237
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS LEE CHANG-HO 4-DAN

52:39.114 --> 52:40.490
COUNTDOWN

52:41.199 --> 52:42.325
[clicks]

52:42.993 --> 52:44.870
[music continues]

52:44.953 --> 52:46.663
[stones clattering]

52:58.800 --> 52:59.676
[lighter clicks]

53:06.892 --> 53:08.685
[cameras clicking]

53:27.537 --> 53:28.413
Hey, let's see.

53:28.496 --> 53:30.498
[reporter] Pro Cheon,
how many moves have been made?

53:30.582 --> 53:32.584
[Pro Cheon] Just a sec. Reporters, please!

53:32.667 --> 53:34.085
I haven't taken a look at it yet.

53:34.169 --> 53:35.754
Ack, later, please! People!

53:35.837 --> 53:37.172
-Sure! Sure!
-[clamoring continues]

53:37.255 --> 53:39.674
Yeah, later, later. Okay. All right.

53:39.758 --> 53:40.800
Jeez.

53:40.884 --> 53:42.093
Ugh, it's so hectic.

53:43.887 --> 53:46.598
Whoa, it's a fierce opening
from Champion Cho.

53:46.681 --> 53:49.392
See? It's an onslaught from the beginning.

53:49.893 --> 53:54.356
Oh my. He's being so ruthless
against his young student. Right?

53:54.439 --> 53:56.816
-[Pro Lee] That's really brutal of him.
-Huh.

53:56.900 --> 53:58.902
[pensive music playing]

54:13.166 --> 54:14.709
TIME SPENT

54:14.793 --> 54:17.921
LEE CHANG-HO 2 HOURS 10 MINUTES
CHO HOON-HYUN 50 MINUTES

54:18.463 --> 54:20.465
[timer ticking]

54:24.886 --> 54:27.180
This game will resume again after lunch.

54:28.848 --> 54:29.933
[ticking stops]

54:31.101 --> 54:32.978
Should I have just taken it?

54:34.271 --> 54:37.023
A knight's jump,
then a two-space extension.

54:39.484 --> 54:41.778
[sighs] Maybe
I should have given up a point.

54:47.909 --> 54:50.704
[clears throat] Great-grandpa,
when did you get here?

54:50.787 --> 54:52.998
Oh, this morning.

54:53.081 --> 54:54.541
Ah. [chuckles]

54:55.709 --> 54:59.421
Oh, but Chang-ho seems off his game today.

54:59.504 --> 55:02.424
Oh, he was ruthless playing
against me last time. [chuckles]

55:02.507 --> 55:04.009
What's this discrimination about?

55:04.092 --> 55:05.218
[both chuckle]

55:05.302 --> 55:09.597
Oh, ask Seonsaengnim to go easy on you,
cut you some slack. [laughs]

55:09.681 --> 55:12.392
What are you talking about?
A match is a match.

55:17.814 --> 55:19.274
He is such a…

55:21.484 --> 55:23.361
Oh, good, food's here. [chuckles]

55:23.445 --> 55:25.447
[chuckling]

55:26.614 --> 55:29.284
Oh, careful, this is hot. It's hot.

55:29.367 --> 55:30.327
Oh, oh, oh.

55:30.410 --> 55:33.246
-[man] Hey, waitress!
-[woman] Some water, please.

55:33.330 --> 55:34.539
[Hoon-hyun grunts]

55:35.123 --> 55:36.416
[dishes clatter]

55:40.503 --> 55:42.505
[water boiling]

55:48.345 --> 55:49.554
[stones clattering]

55:49.637 --> 55:50.597
[stone clacks on board]

55:50.680 --> 55:52.682
[stones clattering]

56:05.403 --> 56:06.738
[paper flipping]

56:10.367 --> 56:12.369
[flipping loudly]

56:15.372 --> 56:17.040
[coughing]

56:19.793 --> 56:21.711
[exhaust fan whirring noisily]

56:21.795 --> 56:24.005
[water boiling loudly]

56:25.507 --> 56:27.675
[emphasized ticking]

56:27.759 --> 56:29.761
-[tense music playing]
-[ticking fast]

56:31.638 --> 56:33.098
[Chang- ho exhales]

56:36.810 --> 56:37.727
[sighs]

56:40.688 --> 56:42.273
[inhales deeply]

56:42.357 --> 56:44.109
[exhales]

56:47.654 --> 56:51.366
Huh, Mr. Chang-ho seems to be making
small mistakes today.

56:51.449 --> 56:55.161
We can't compete with him,
so how could a kid do that?

56:56.663 --> 56:58.623
It's his seonsaengnim. He looks up to him.

56:58.706 --> 57:00.750
[tense music continues]

57:01.584 --> 57:03.586
[stones clicking]

57:19.853 --> 57:21.438
TIME SPENT

57:21.521 --> 57:24.774
LEE CHANG-HO 3 HOURS 51 MINUTES
CHO HOON-HYUN 1 HOUR 43 MINUTES

57:24.858 --> 57:26.860
[music continues]

57:33.199 --> 57:35.994
[Hoon-hyun] Think about something
familiar and comfortable.

57:36.077 --> 57:39.539
Something that just relaxes you
by thinking of it.

57:42.208 --> 57:44.878
The match is over
the moment you lose your composure.

57:44.961 --> 57:46.963
[music continues]

58:01.436 --> 58:04.230
[clocks ticking]

58:04.772 --> 58:06.524
[clock winding]

58:06.608 --> 58:08.610
[clocks continue ticking]

58:23.500 --> 58:25.043
[clock striking]

58:26.085 --> 58:28.254
-[clock striking louder]
-[clock ticking louder]

58:28.338 --> 58:30.173
[ticking and striking echoes]

58:30.256 --> 58:32.258
[ticking and striking stops]

58:32.342 --> 58:34.344
[tense music continues]

59:34.070 --> 59:36.072
[ticking]

59:41.536 --> 59:43.162
[stones clattering]

59:45.206 --> 59:46.207
[beeps]

59:50.336 --> 59:52.630
[music continues]

01:00:03.725 --> 01:00:05.059
TIME SPENT

01:00:05.143 --> 01:00:08.980
LEE CHANG-HO 3 HOURS 53 MINUTES
CHO HOON-HYUN 2 HOURS 58 MINUTES

01:00:09.063 --> 01:00:11.065
[tense music continues]

01:00:36.049 --> 01:00:39.010
[music fades]

01:00:39.677 --> 01:00:40.637
[man] Cho 9-dan.

01:00:41.429 --> 01:00:42.263
One,

01:00:43.097 --> 01:00:43.931
two,

01:00:44.682 --> 01:00:45.516
three,

01:00:46.059 --> 01:00:46.893
four,

01:00:47.685 --> 01:00:48.519
five,

01:00:49.354 --> 01:00:50.188
six,

01:00:51.105 --> 01:00:52.440
-seven…
-[water boiling]

01:00:52.523 --> 01:00:53.441
…eight,

01:00:54.150 --> 01:00:55.026
nine,

01:00:55.652 --> 01:00:56.527
ten.

01:00:56.611 --> 01:00:57.737
TIME SPENT

01:00:57.820 --> 01:00:59.989
LEE CHANG-HO 4 HOURS 50 MINUTES
CHO HOON-HYUN 5 HOURS

01:01:00.073 --> 01:01:02.367
[man] Cho 9-dan,
you have two byoyomi left.

01:01:03.534 --> 01:01:05.828
[inhales deeply]

01:01:05.912 --> 01:01:08.498
[exhales]

01:01:08.581 --> 01:01:10.583
[contemplative music playing]

01:01:16.881 --> 01:01:19.217
[stones clattering]

01:01:28.935 --> 01:01:30.478
[stones clattering]

01:01:35.525 --> 01:01:36.651
[inhales sharply]

01:01:38.027 --> 01:01:39.737
[music continues]

01:01:45.118 --> 01:01:46.244
[stone clatters]

01:01:54.001 --> 01:01:56.003
[gulping]

01:01:58.589 --> 01:01:59.590
[glass thuds on table]

01:02:00.383 --> 01:02:01.551
[sighs]

01:02:04.470 --> 01:02:05.888
[sighs loudly]

01:02:09.976 --> 01:02:10.852
[stone clatters]

01:02:11.936 --> 01:02:13.771
[sighs loudly, laughs]

01:02:13.855 --> 01:02:16.065
[man] I don't know.
We'll know when it ends.

01:02:16.149 --> 01:02:18.484
-[Gi-cheol] If this goes right…
-[Pro Lee] Huh?

01:02:18.568 --> 01:02:20.987
[exhales] …we might see a real coup here.

01:02:21.070 --> 01:02:21.988
A coup d'état?

01:02:22.739 --> 01:02:24.365
-Really?
-[man] Coup d'état?

01:02:25.366 --> 01:02:27.744
Oh, let's not do this.
Let's go see for ourselves.

01:02:27.827 --> 01:02:29.746
-[clamoring]
-Hurry up! Hurry!

01:02:29.829 --> 01:02:31.581
-Run! Run! Run!
-What's going on?

01:02:32.248 --> 01:02:34.167
Let me see! Let me see!

01:02:34.250 --> 01:02:35.668
Let me see! Let me see!

01:02:35.752 --> 01:02:37.712
[clamoring]

01:02:37.795 --> 01:02:40.173
-[speaking indistinctly]
-[man shushing] Quiet.

01:02:40.757 --> 01:02:41.966
[man shushing]

01:02:42.049 --> 01:02:43.718
[tense music playing]

01:02:51.476 --> 01:02:52.560
Is it done?

01:02:52.643 --> 01:02:54.645
[music continues]

01:03:15.750 --> 01:03:17.460
[Pro Cheon] Black wins by half a point!

01:03:17.543 --> 01:03:19.378
At 271 moves!

01:03:19.462 --> 01:03:21.464
Hey, no, I said black.

01:03:21.547 --> 01:03:24.634
Listen! It's Lee Chang-ho that won!

01:03:24.717 --> 01:03:25.718
[camera clicks]

01:03:25.802 --> 01:03:27.804
[contemplative music continues]

01:03:42.276 --> 01:03:43.736
[music fades]

01:03:43.820 --> 01:03:47.490
Um, it's so late.
The restaurants will be closing soon.

01:03:49.951 --> 01:03:51.285
-Champion Cho.
-Huh?

01:03:52.119 --> 01:03:53.913
-[sighs]
-[people murmuring]

01:03:53.996 --> 01:03:56.123
[inhales deeply]

01:03:57.375 --> 01:03:59.377
[exhales]

01:04:01.170 --> 01:04:03.130
A word for your student, and his victory?

01:04:03.214 --> 01:04:04.882
Champion Cho, can I get a comment?

01:04:09.554 --> 01:04:12.765
I've got nothing more to teach him.

01:04:12.849 --> 01:04:14.934
-He can go his own way now.
-[reporter chuckles]

01:04:15.017 --> 01:04:16.894
Where do you think the match went wrong?

01:04:16.978 --> 01:04:18.646
-Excuse me.
-[reporter 2] Uh, Champion Cho!

01:04:18.729 --> 01:04:21.065
You'll likely face Lee 4-dan
in the Kisei too.

01:04:21.148 --> 01:04:24.110
How do you plan to prepare for that match,
Champion Cho?

01:04:32.535 --> 01:04:35.037
First of all, congratulations.
How are you feeling?

01:04:36.289 --> 01:04:37.874
I'm sorry to my seonsaengnim…

01:04:39.500 --> 01:04:41.002
I won with a bad game.

01:04:53.514 --> 01:04:55.516
[somber music playing]

01:05:07.862 --> 01:05:09.864
[exhales shakily]

01:05:20.833 --> 01:05:22.752
[dog barking in distance]

01:05:33.220 --> 01:05:34.555
[Hoon-hyun's wife] You're late.

01:05:35.139 --> 01:05:36.140
[exhales]

01:05:38.351 --> 01:05:39.602
How did it go?

01:05:43.981 --> 01:05:45.149
[door closes]

01:05:49.987 --> 01:05:51.238
[chuckles]

01:05:51.989 --> 01:05:53.616
Chang-ho, you did so well.

01:05:54.158 --> 01:05:55.034
Congrats.

01:05:56.160 --> 01:05:57.119
Thank you, Auntie.

01:05:57.828 --> 01:05:59.580
Yes, good work, all right?

01:06:00.081 --> 01:06:02.416
You must be exhausted. Go rest.

01:06:02.500 --> 01:06:03.459
Okay.

01:06:13.844 --> 01:06:15.054
[Chang-ho] Grandpa.

01:06:16.472 --> 01:06:17.974
Did you see me win today?

01:06:20.267 --> 01:06:21.352
You know, I…

01:06:22.645 --> 01:06:24.397
wanted to win so much.

01:06:26.983 --> 01:06:28.275
Through my own style.

01:06:29.026 --> 01:06:31.028
[inhales shakily]

01:06:32.113 --> 01:06:33.656
[sobbing]

01:06:34.573 --> 01:06:35.491
[sniffles]

01:06:37.368 --> 01:06:39.370
[sobbing]

01:06:49.672 --> 01:06:51.215
[exhales]

01:06:58.764 --> 01:07:00.099
[music fades]

01:07:00.182 --> 01:07:01.308
[bicycle bell rings]

01:07:07.606 --> 01:07:09.316
A HALF-POINT WIN
SENSATION IN THE WORLD OF GO

01:07:09.400 --> 01:07:10.568
YOUNGEST CHAMP, LEE CHANG-HO

01:07:10.651 --> 01:07:12.319
[groans]

01:07:12.403 --> 01:07:13.863
That boy, well… [sighs]

01:07:16.198 --> 01:07:18.200
[stones clattering]

01:07:20.619 --> 01:07:21.662
[Hoon-hyun exhales]

01:07:46.020 --> 01:07:47.521
Should I have wedged it?

01:07:51.358 --> 01:07:52.651
[sighs]

01:07:54.653 --> 01:07:56.322
[inhales deeply]

01:07:56.405 --> 01:07:57.448
[sighs loudly]

01:07:59.366 --> 01:08:00.743
-[knocking on door]
-[gasps]

01:08:02.620 --> 01:08:03.454
Oh.

01:08:03.954 --> 01:08:05.039
Seonsaengnim.

01:08:07.166 --> 01:08:08.876
Um, our review?

01:08:10.127 --> 01:08:11.128
Oh, yes. We should.

01:08:11.212 --> 01:08:13.297
REVIEW: TO REPLAY A FINISHED GAME
AND GO OVER THE MOVES

01:08:13.380 --> 01:08:16.133
Weather's good. Let's go out there.

01:08:16.884 --> 01:08:18.052
[stone clacks on board]

01:08:20.137 --> 01:08:23.307
What if I defend right here?

01:08:23.891 --> 01:08:25.309
That's not bad either,

01:08:28.479 --> 01:08:29.688
but here is better…

01:08:29.772 --> 01:08:31.148
[stones clattering]

01:08:33.859 --> 01:08:36.237
…and expand the center.

01:08:36.320 --> 01:08:37.363
The black's heavy.

01:08:39.240 --> 01:08:40.783
[exhales]

01:08:43.244 --> 01:08:44.328
[inhales sharply]

01:08:44.411 --> 01:08:45.371
Or maybe…

01:08:49.458 --> 01:08:51.252
if I wedge it like this?

01:08:51.919 --> 01:08:54.547
[breathes deeply]

01:08:55.548 --> 01:08:56.966
[inhales deeply]

01:08:57.049 --> 01:08:57.967
Mmm…

01:09:00.678 --> 01:09:02.221
[inhales sharply] Uh…

01:09:02.304 --> 01:09:03.472
[exhales]

01:09:05.141 --> 01:09:08.435
Hmm. That shape doesn't look good there.

01:09:09.061 --> 01:09:12.148
You could defend this side instead. Here.

01:09:12.231 --> 01:09:15.317
Or maybe attach it over here first.

01:09:17.695 --> 01:09:21.407
I don't think this is bad right here.

01:09:21.490 --> 01:09:24.743
We could do atari here, push through,

01:09:26.912 --> 01:09:27.872
and attach.

01:09:27.955 --> 01:09:30.875
No, not there. It's going
to leave a bad aftertaste.

01:09:30.958 --> 01:09:32.084
[stone clacks on board]

01:09:32.168 --> 01:09:34.086
And no need to look further here.

01:09:35.504 --> 01:09:37.047
[sighs]

01:09:38.465 --> 01:09:39.341
Seonsaengnim.

01:09:39.925 --> 01:09:41.927
[breathes deeply]

01:09:43.888 --> 01:09:44.722
[inhales deeply]

01:09:45.472 --> 01:09:46.473
I'm sorry.

01:09:47.391 --> 01:09:49.810
About yesterday.

01:09:52.104 --> 01:09:52.938
What?

01:09:57.151 --> 01:09:58.944
When I'm across the board.

01:10:00.988 --> 01:10:02.740
Am I seonsaengnim to you?

01:10:04.491 --> 01:10:05.659
Uh, no.

01:10:07.411 --> 01:10:08.329
You're my enemy.

01:10:08.412 --> 01:10:10.873
Winning a game doesn't mean
the world has changed.

01:10:12.249 --> 01:10:13.584
Don't become deluded.

01:10:14.251 --> 01:10:17.254
Go professionals win and lose every day,
and that's our fate.

01:10:17.338 --> 01:10:18.339
Arrogant punk.

01:10:20.549 --> 01:10:23.427
From now on, let's not review
games we've played.

01:10:29.391 --> 01:10:30.559
[door opens, closes]

01:10:32.102 --> 01:10:34.438
[breathing deeply]

01:10:35.314 --> 01:10:36.690
[groans]

01:10:36.774 --> 01:10:40.819
[breathing heavily]

01:10:52.039 --> 01:10:53.123
[sighs]

01:10:54.917 --> 01:10:56.210
[exhales]

01:11:02.091 --> 01:11:03.133
[exhales]

01:11:06.845 --> 01:11:08.847
[dramatic music playing]

01:11:10.266 --> 01:11:12.309
FOURTH KISEI CHALLENGE MATCH
LAST ROUND

01:11:12.393 --> 01:11:14.937
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS LEE CHANG-HO 6-DAN

01:11:15.020 --> 01:11:17.314
[Pro Cheon]
It's the 27th game between them.

01:11:17.398 --> 01:11:19.024
It's a world-shaking event

01:11:19.108 --> 01:11:21.568
that will go down in Korean Go history.

01:11:21.652 --> 01:11:23.237
It's unprecedented.

01:11:23.320 --> 01:11:25.906
Yes. The Daewang, the Kisei,

01:11:25.990 --> 01:11:28.826
the Paewang, the Choegowi,
and now, Kiwang.

01:11:28.909 --> 01:11:30.577
THE 33RD CHOEGOWI CHALLENGE MATCH
LAST ROUND

01:11:30.661 --> 01:11:34.039
The student and the teacher are meeting
for the finals of all five cups.

01:11:34.123 --> 01:11:36.834
[Pro Baek] This is all
because of Lee Chang-ho 6-dan.

01:11:36.917 --> 01:11:38.460
He's moving so quickly.

01:11:38.544 --> 01:11:41.463
Cho 9-dan probably didn't expect him
to rise so quickly, either.

01:11:41.547 --> 01:11:45.342
[moderator] Recent games have shown
Cho 9-dan backed into a corner.

01:11:45.426 --> 01:11:48.554
Cho 9-dan's knife
is famous for its sharpness.

01:11:48.637 --> 01:11:50.639
It penetrates your weak spots mercilessly.

01:11:51.223 --> 01:11:52.224
But it seems

01:11:52.891 --> 01:11:55.019
it's not working on Lee Chang-ho 6-dan.

01:11:55.102 --> 01:11:59.440
Yes, Mr. Lee 6-dan lets
his opponents do as they like.

01:11:59.523 --> 01:12:02.568
But, when they're done,
and they realize they've lost,

01:12:02.651 --> 01:12:04.486
it leaves them dumbstruck.

01:12:04.570 --> 01:12:08.866
[Pro Baek] One professional player told me
he's scared to face Cho 9-dan.

01:12:08.949 --> 01:12:12.453
As for Chang-ho,
he doesn't even want to look at him.

01:12:12.536 --> 01:12:16.540
[Pro Cheon] As everyone knows, the two
have completely different styles of play.

01:12:16.623 --> 01:12:18.542
The teacher is fast,
and the student is slow.

01:12:18.625 --> 01:12:21.045
The student holds, and the teacher fights.

01:12:21.712 --> 01:12:23.797
Looking only at recent games,

01:12:23.881 --> 01:12:26.759
they seem to have switched their styles.

01:12:26.842 --> 01:12:30.095
It is now the teacher who's on the defense

01:12:30.679 --> 01:12:32.639
while the student is on the offense.

01:12:32.723 --> 01:12:36.852
[moderator] Cho 9-dan must be struggling
immensely to change this trend.

01:12:36.935 --> 01:12:40.898
I agree, but the problem is,
Lee Chang-ho isn't just good at defense.

01:12:41.648 --> 01:12:43.817
He was absolutely ruthless yesterday.

01:12:44.401 --> 01:12:48.405
Cho Hoon-hyun, Go's best,
hasn't once extended his hand.

01:12:48.489 --> 01:12:51.241
-[reporter 1] Could I have a comment?
-[reporter 2] Cho 9-dan!

01:12:51.325 --> 01:12:53.410
-[reporter 3] Sir! Sir!
-[reporter 4] Cho 9-dan!

01:12:53.494 --> 01:12:55.829
[reporter 5] Lee 6-dan,
first of all, congratulations.

01:12:55.913 --> 01:12:57.706
Could you tell us how you're feeling?

01:12:57.790 --> 01:12:59.958
[reporters clamoring]

01:13:00.042 --> 01:13:02.628
[moderator] There's only
the Paewang left now.

01:13:02.711 --> 01:13:06.840
If Cho 9-dan loses there,
he'll have won no cups.

01:13:06.924 --> 01:13:07.758
GO SPECIAL FORUM

01:13:07.841 --> 01:13:11.553
So how do you all think that
the next upcoming game will go?

01:13:11.637 --> 01:13:13.555
[Pro Cheon]
Lee Chang-ho is in great spirits,

01:13:14.098 --> 01:13:16.600
but this is Cho Hoon-hyun, the King of Go.

01:13:16.683 --> 01:13:18.352
You can see
he won't back down easily here.

01:13:18.435 --> 01:13:19.853
Yes, that's right.

01:13:19.937 --> 01:13:22.272
Mr. Fujisawa 9-dan of Japan,

01:13:22.356 --> 01:13:25.401
this man won himself a cup
when he was well into his sixties.

01:13:25.484 --> 01:13:27.486
Oh, let's not be daft here.

01:13:28.654 --> 01:13:30.531
There wasn't a Lee Chang-ho in Japan!

01:13:30.614 --> 01:13:32.699
WINS THE YING SHIBEI CUP!
UNIFIES THE WORLD!

01:13:32.783 --> 01:13:34.785
[dramatic music playing]

01:13:36.787 --> 01:13:38.497
Lee Chang-ho is changing
the paradigm of Go.

01:13:38.580 --> 01:13:40.457
LEE CHANG-HO, NEW STYLE OF PLAY AND MOVES

01:13:40.541 --> 01:13:42.334
This is what the fans of Go are saying.

01:13:42.418 --> 01:13:47.005
Go is a sport where you can fight all day,
only for Lee Chang-ho to win in the end.

01:13:47.089 --> 01:13:48.173
[stones clatter]

01:13:48.257 --> 01:13:49.883
[huffing]

01:13:49.967 --> 01:13:53.053
ETERNAL KINGDOM FALLEN BY HALF-POINT
CHO ON THE EDGE OF A CLIFF

01:13:53.137 --> 01:13:55.264
29TH PAEWANG CHALLENGE MATCH
FOURTH ROUND

01:13:55.347 --> 01:13:57.933
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS LEE CHANG-HO 6-DAN

01:13:59.017 --> 01:14:00.185
[stones clattering]

01:14:00.978 --> 01:14:02.980
[music continues]

01:14:09.445 --> 01:14:12.156
[breathing heavily]

01:14:14.908 --> 01:14:15.909
[music fades]

01:14:25.085 --> 01:14:26.086
[grunts]

01:14:32.259 --> 01:14:33.927
-Oh.
-Champion Cho!

01:14:34.428 --> 01:14:36.555
-Over there, tissue. Please, tissue.
-Oh.

01:14:38.307 --> 01:14:40.309
[breathing heavily]

01:14:44.354 --> 01:14:46.023
[birds chirping]

01:14:50.819 --> 01:14:53.947
Cho seonsaengnim. We'll be heading out.

01:14:54.531 --> 01:14:57.159
[Hoon-hyun's wife]
Oh, yes. Have a safe trip home.

01:15:06.418 --> 01:15:08.921
[sighs] Terrible situation.

01:15:10.380 --> 01:15:11.965
For you and for Chang-ho.

01:15:12.049 --> 01:15:14.551
[breathes deeply]

01:15:22.684 --> 01:15:23.977
[slurping]

01:15:33.946 --> 01:15:35.113
Stomach bothering you?

01:15:39.034 --> 01:15:40.160
I feel awful.

01:15:41.828 --> 01:15:43.455
For my seonsaengnim, you know.

01:15:45.916 --> 01:15:47.167
Also for my Auntie.

01:15:50.462 --> 01:15:51.338
Well…

01:15:53.006 --> 01:15:54.550
would you rather lose?

01:16:01.848 --> 01:16:03.475
Then give it your best and win.

01:16:04.851 --> 01:16:06.353
What else can you do?

01:16:10.566 --> 01:16:12.734
-[footsteps treading]
-[dog barking in distance]

01:16:18.865 --> 01:16:19.741
[sighs]

01:16:40.429 --> 01:16:42.180
[exhales] You're back?

01:16:46.476 --> 01:16:47.811
[Hoon-hyun sighs]

01:16:49.980 --> 01:16:51.481
[exhales]

01:16:53.525 --> 01:16:55.694
There was a time
you couldn't tie your shoes,

01:16:56.194 --> 01:16:59.031
but now you're a professional.

01:17:06.413 --> 01:17:07.414
It's time

01:17:09.750 --> 01:17:11.168
for you to stand alone.

01:17:13.211 --> 01:17:15.130
You've surpassed me already.

01:17:16.798 --> 01:17:19.343
It makes no sense
to keep you as my student.

01:17:21.094 --> 01:17:22.220
I'm not there yet.

01:17:22.304 --> 01:17:25.349
There's still so much I don't know
that I should be learning from you.

01:17:25.432 --> 01:17:27.976
[sighs] Well, not from me.

01:17:31.563 --> 01:17:34.066
I really should have sent you away
much sooner.

01:17:38.779 --> 01:17:41.365
Though winning and losing
is a part of our lives,

01:17:44.034 --> 01:17:46.036
it's been hard for both of us,

01:17:47.913 --> 01:17:49.581
living in the same house,

01:17:51.708 --> 01:17:53.043
fighting across the board.

01:17:54.961 --> 01:17:56.963
I'm sorry, seonsaengnim.

01:17:58.965 --> 01:18:00.008
I didn't teach you that.

01:18:02.594 --> 01:18:06.098
The pro's job is to win,
no matter the opponent.

01:18:12.938 --> 01:18:14.398
[sighs]

01:18:14.481 --> 01:18:16.692
You've taught me a lot
these days, as well.

01:18:18.402 --> 01:18:20.654
I'm learning
that I can lose at any time, now.

01:18:25.826 --> 01:18:27.828
[breathes deeply]

01:18:28.745 --> 01:18:30.080
You'll do fine without me,

01:18:31.540 --> 01:18:33.291
but after you leave, don't be lazy.

01:18:36.795 --> 01:18:39.673
[breathes deeply]

01:18:48.432 --> 01:18:49.683
Thinking about it,

01:18:51.560 --> 01:18:56.273
I never once complimented you
in all this time you've been here with us.

01:18:59.568 --> 01:19:00.819
Your seonsaengnim…

01:19:03.697 --> 01:19:05.449
has always been very proud of you.

01:19:08.410 --> 01:19:09.411
You were…

01:19:12.038 --> 01:19:13.165
always my pride.

01:19:18.879 --> 01:19:19.796
[door opens]

01:19:22.215 --> 01:19:23.216
[door closes]

01:19:23.300 --> 01:19:25.886
-[emotional music playing]
-[breathing emotionally]

01:19:32.893 --> 01:19:34.686
Here's yeolmu kimchi for you.

01:19:35.187 --> 01:19:36.354
Uh, Chang-ho really likes it.

01:19:36.438 --> 01:19:37.939
Oh, thank you.

01:19:39.024 --> 01:19:40.025
[man] Okay, we're done.

01:19:42.068 --> 01:19:43.069
Chang-ho.

01:19:43.987 --> 01:19:45.363
Let me have a big hug.

01:19:46.615 --> 01:19:49.576
Eat well, okay? Come visit us too.

01:19:51.995 --> 01:19:53.538
I will. Thanks, Auntie.

01:19:54.247 --> 01:19:56.249
[emotional music continues]

01:20:01.588 --> 01:20:05.592
[Hoon-hyun's wife] Dress warmly.
Come by for side dishes when you run out.

01:20:05.675 --> 01:20:07.552
[man 1] Sir, thank you so much
for everything.

01:20:08.178 --> 01:20:09.221
[man 2] It was nothing.

01:20:09.304 --> 01:20:10.639
[man 1] Please, be well.

01:20:10.722 --> 01:20:13.058
[man 2] Yes, you too. Have a safe journey.

01:20:16.645 --> 01:20:17.646
Seonsaengnim.

01:20:24.820 --> 01:20:27.697
Thank you so much for everything.

01:20:28.406 --> 01:20:29.741
Oh…

01:20:39.751 --> 01:20:42.295
Your seonsaengnim gave this to you.

01:20:59.271 --> 01:21:02.148
WHITE CHO HYEON-SIK VS BLACK LEE CHANG-HO
BLACK WINS BY 1.5 POINTS

01:21:02.232 --> 01:21:04.234
[emotional music continues]

01:21:08.613 --> 01:21:10.615
[sobbing]

01:21:42.022 --> 01:21:44.399
[man] The Great Cho Hoon-hyun
without a single cup.

01:21:44.482 --> 01:21:47.986
[scoffs] He's getting devoured
by the tiger cub he raised.

01:21:48.069 --> 01:21:49.321
-Who can he blame?
-[urinating]

01:21:49.404 --> 01:21:50.947
Still, it must sting.

01:21:51.031 --> 01:21:55.702
Yeah, we make more money when the matches
are basically neck-and-neck,

01:21:55.785 --> 01:21:57.078
and not like this, huh?

01:21:57.162 --> 01:21:58.914
We won't make much commission this way.

01:21:59.748 --> 01:22:02.334
On Chang-ho, let's lower the payout.

01:22:03.752 --> 01:22:08.548
One, two, three, four, five…

01:22:08.632 --> 01:22:11.468
19TH KIWANG FINALS
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS NAM GI-CHEOL 9-DAN

01:22:11.551 --> 01:22:13.929
-…six, seven, eight, nine, ten.
-[breathes deeply]

01:22:16.097 --> 01:22:17.933
Cho 9-dan, runs out of time.

01:22:18.725 --> 01:22:20.936
Nam 9-dan wins by default.

01:22:21.937 --> 01:22:22.854
[clicks]

01:22:22.938 --> 01:22:24.648
[breathes deeply]

01:22:38.244 --> 01:22:39.788
[door opens]

01:22:43.333 --> 01:22:44.250
[door closes]

01:22:49.297 --> 01:22:50.173
The kids?

01:22:51.091 --> 01:22:52.884
-Not home yet?
-Mm-mm.

01:22:54.177 --> 01:22:55.261
How was the game?

01:22:56.680 --> 01:22:57.847
I lost.

01:22:59.015 --> 01:23:00.809
I'll live with you if you lose…

01:23:02.018 --> 01:23:03.395
but not if you're pathetic.

01:23:04.437 --> 01:23:06.982
[inhales deeply]
Stop running from what's real.

01:23:09.985 --> 01:23:11.444
I never resented either of you

01:23:12.404 --> 01:23:15.156
during all of those years
we took care of Chang-ho.

01:23:16.700 --> 01:23:18.201
But seeing you like this…

01:23:19.369 --> 01:23:20.787
I'm resenting him now.

01:23:23.456 --> 01:23:25.375
[sighs] Don't be pathetic.

01:23:28.420 --> 01:23:29.504
[whirring]

01:23:32.132 --> 01:23:33.008
Ah.

01:23:34.175 --> 01:23:37.053
Oh. Hey, Champion Lee,
it's been a long time! [chuckles]

01:23:37.137 --> 01:23:38.013
You eat?

01:23:38.513 --> 01:23:40.849
Well, if you didn't,
let's go get something.

01:23:40.932 --> 01:23:43.393
No thanks, I'm not really hungry yet.

01:23:43.476 --> 01:23:44.978
[Pro Baek] I'm sure he's full.

01:23:45.061 --> 01:23:48.189
He's gorged himself
on all those championship titles,

01:23:48.273 --> 01:23:50.233
and devoured his seonsaengnim. [scoffs]

01:23:50.316 --> 01:23:52.986
Hey, what do you mean he devoured him?
You take that back.

01:23:53.069 --> 01:23:55.488
Why are you getting so upset?

01:23:56.990 --> 01:23:58.408
Why don't you laugh?

01:23:58.491 --> 01:23:59.451
It's a joke.

01:23:59.534 --> 01:24:00.618
[laughs]

01:24:01.786 --> 01:24:02.912
[sighs]

01:24:02.996 --> 01:24:06.166
Oh, it must be nice, Pro Lee, huh?
Wow. You're photogenic too.

01:24:06.249 --> 01:24:08.084
THE STUDENT WHO STABBED
HIS TEACHER IN THE BACK

01:24:08.168 --> 01:24:09.753
ANOTHER FORFEIT
WILL CHO HOON-HYUN RETIRE?

01:24:10.587 --> 01:24:13.131
[man] Wow, you could be a model, really.

01:24:13.214 --> 01:24:15.216
[phone ringing in distance]

01:24:16.968 --> 01:24:19.721
-Why don't we have intestine soup?
-[stones rattling]

01:24:19.804 --> 01:24:21.222
-It's been a while.
-Mmm, okay.

01:24:21.306 --> 01:24:24.184
-How about a drink to go with it?
-Well, then what should I do?

01:24:29.105 --> 01:24:29.939
Huh?

01:24:30.732 --> 01:24:33.485
Pro Baek, if you were me,
what would you do?

01:24:34.944 --> 01:24:36.404
Should I just lose?

01:24:37.113 --> 01:24:39.866
Hey. [chuckles]
What are you asking me for?

01:24:39.949 --> 01:24:40.784
[chuckles]

01:24:40.867 --> 01:24:46.081
That's what I was taught.
That a pro's job is to win.

01:24:47.957 --> 01:24:51.294
You must not have ever met a good teacher
to learn from yet, Pro Baek.

01:24:51.377 --> 01:24:52.670
You're such a…

01:24:53.922 --> 01:24:55.757
Your mouth is getting ahead of you now.

01:24:57.509 --> 01:24:58.635
You're not laughing.

01:24:59.677 --> 01:25:01.221
I was joking a bit, too.

01:25:01.304 --> 01:25:02.514
What?

01:25:04.182 --> 01:25:06.101
A joke. He's joking.

01:25:06.726 --> 01:25:08.436
Champion Lee, let's go. Come on.

01:25:11.606 --> 01:25:12.565
[tsks]

01:25:14.526 --> 01:25:16.945
A forfeit? The Great Cho Hoon-hyun?

01:25:17.529 --> 01:25:19.948
-You should have at least shown up!
-[Hoon-hyun] Hmm.

01:25:20.031 --> 01:25:22.367
[Pro Cheon] Do you know how much
your wife worries about you?

01:25:23.701 --> 01:25:24.702
And Chang-ho?

01:25:24.786 --> 01:25:26.704
He doesn't talk about it,

01:25:27.539 --> 01:25:30.083
but think of how uncomfortable this is
for him as well.

01:25:30.166 --> 01:25:32.252
[rain pattering]

01:25:34.879 --> 01:25:36.881
[gentle music playing]

01:25:38.049 --> 01:25:40.802
Hey, what are you doing that for?
You're a lightweight.

01:25:43.763 --> 01:25:45.306
Hey, Champion Cho.

01:25:46.391 --> 01:25:47.225
Huh?

01:25:47.725 --> 01:25:49.727
[gulping]

01:25:51.396 --> 01:25:52.272
[Pro Lee scoffs]

01:25:53.314 --> 01:25:54.274
[glass thuds on table]

01:25:56.359 --> 01:25:57.610
[exhales]

01:25:57.694 --> 01:25:59.362
My knife's rusted.

01:26:00.780 --> 01:26:01.739
[glass thuds on table]

01:26:04.200 --> 01:26:06.202
Hold on. You don't have an umbrella.

01:26:06.286 --> 01:26:07.662
Hey, Champion Cho!

01:26:08.246 --> 01:26:10.373
[music continues]

01:26:10.456 --> 01:26:11.624
[exhales]

01:26:12.709 --> 01:26:13.585
[gags]

01:26:21.801 --> 01:26:23.094
[retching]

01:26:27.223 --> 01:26:28.099
[groans]

01:26:29.142 --> 01:26:30.101
[groans]

01:26:30.185 --> 01:26:31.060
[retching]

01:26:33.980 --> 01:26:35.773
[grunts, groans]

01:26:37.442 --> 01:26:39.819
[grunting softly]

01:26:40.778 --> 01:26:41.613
[exhales]

01:26:54.542 --> 01:26:56.878
CHO HOON-HYUN VS LEE CHANG-HO
NO-COUNT WIN BY LEE

01:26:57.921 --> 01:26:58.755
[clears throat]

01:26:58.838 --> 01:27:00.298
[papers rustling]

01:27:00.381 --> 01:27:02.383
[rain pattering]

01:27:11.559 --> 01:27:15.313
[tuts] I'd be upset if you bowed down
to something as small as this.

01:27:18.775 --> 01:27:21.986
You have stabbed me
at least a hundred times now, in my back.

01:27:22.070 --> 01:27:24.072
[sighs]

01:27:25.323 --> 01:27:27.408
Everyone hurts when they've been punched.

01:27:28.493 --> 01:27:30.995
[tuts] Chang-ho must have it hard.

01:27:33.456 --> 01:27:34.999
The poor kid's suffering.

01:27:36.417 --> 01:27:38.002
He met the wrong teacher.

01:27:39.712 --> 01:27:42.924
He can't even try to laugh
even while he's winning.

01:27:44.425 --> 01:27:46.219
He's not done learning from you.

01:27:48.054 --> 01:27:51.057
You need to challenge him,
so that he'll grow stronger.

01:27:53.726 --> 01:27:55.436
The game of Go is so odd.

01:27:58.106 --> 01:27:59.524
Once you place a stone,

01:28:00.900 --> 01:28:02.610
you feel like you can do it,

01:28:04.904 --> 01:28:06.823
but the first stone is the hardest.

01:28:11.411 --> 01:28:13.913
I thought
I understood the game, but… [sighs]

01:28:16.374 --> 01:28:18.293
You have to endure that, to win.

01:28:20.253 --> 01:28:24.090
The wound oozes, scabs over,
and then new flesh covers the wound.

01:28:25.758 --> 01:28:27.010
You keep biting down,

01:28:29.679 --> 01:28:31.306
and you'll find an opportunity.

01:28:34.934 --> 01:28:36.227
Champion Cho.

01:28:38.730 --> 01:28:41.232
Once you start avoiding
your opponent on the board,

01:28:44.277 --> 01:28:45.903
there's nowhere left to go.

01:28:45.987 --> 01:28:47.989
[gentle music continues]

01:28:57.874 --> 01:28:59.167
Act like yourself.

01:29:00.543 --> 01:29:02.086
Being small and quiet

01:29:03.838 --> 01:29:05.256
does not suit you at all.

01:29:06.049 --> 01:29:08.051
[music continues]

01:29:15.475 --> 01:29:16.476
[music fades]

01:29:21.564 --> 01:29:23.566
[hopeful music playing]

01:29:45.505 --> 01:29:46.589
[exhales]

01:29:48.800 --> 01:29:51.677
GO IS ABOUT TRYING TO FIND AN ANSWER
WHEN THERE ARE NO ANSWERS

01:29:51.761 --> 01:29:53.554
KENSAKU SEGOE (CHO HOON-HYUN'S MASTER)

01:29:56.391 --> 01:29:57.558
[sighs]

01:29:58.768 --> 01:30:00.770
[music continues]

01:30:15.451 --> 01:30:20.289
GO IS A FIGHT AGAINST YOURSELF
JULY 1964, CHO HOON-HYUN

01:30:21.582 --> 01:30:22.625
[chuckles softly]

01:30:24.001 --> 01:30:26.587
[man] Oh, I'm full. That was great.

01:30:26.671 --> 01:30:28.840
Pro Baek, early congrats on your win.

01:30:28.923 --> 01:30:30.800
I didn't see Champion Cho today.

01:30:30.883 --> 01:30:33.719
Don't congratulate me. This leaves
a bad taste even when I win.

01:30:33.803 --> 01:30:37.765
Ugh, now's the moment to face off
against Cho Hoon-hyun and crush him.

01:30:37.849 --> 01:30:39.058
[men laugh]

01:30:39.142 --> 01:30:41.310
-He's scared and lost his nerve.
-He's off the deep end.

01:30:41.394 --> 01:30:42.478
[laughing]

01:30:42.562 --> 01:30:43.688
[stops laughing]

01:30:43.771 --> 01:30:45.398
[paper rustling]

01:30:45.481 --> 01:30:47.942
[Hoon-hyun] Oh, Pro Baek, you've arrived.

01:30:48.693 --> 01:30:49.694
So,

01:30:50.778 --> 01:30:52.238
have you had a good meal, sir?

01:30:52.905 --> 01:30:53.990
[spits out toothpick]

01:30:54.782 --> 01:30:55.783
[indistinct chatter]

01:30:55.867 --> 01:31:00.705
ONE YEAR LATER

01:31:05.626 --> 01:31:07.712
SECOND WOMEN'S GUKSU CUP FINALS

01:31:07.795 --> 01:31:09.255
Huh? Seonsaengnim.

01:31:10.256 --> 01:31:12.717
Oh, you. Hey, let me help you with that.

01:31:12.800 --> 01:31:15.553
Oh, no, it's okay. I'll do it.

01:31:18.139 --> 01:31:19.140
[grunts]

01:31:25.188 --> 01:31:26.105
Seonsaengnim.

01:31:27.773 --> 01:31:28.816
Today's game…

01:31:29.734 --> 01:31:32.111
You're embarrassing. Wow. [chuckles]

01:31:32.612 --> 01:31:35.114
Punk, I won. Oh man.

01:31:36.908 --> 01:31:40.077
Aigo! Look at me, in the preliminaries.

01:31:40.661 --> 01:31:41.537
[scoffs]

01:31:42.079 --> 01:31:43.873
I saw your latest game.

01:31:44.790 --> 01:31:47.793
You still won't put up a fight, will you?

01:31:48.920 --> 01:31:51.047
Because I can win without fighting.

01:31:52.590 --> 01:31:56.010
So why should I risk it by fighting?

01:31:56.511 --> 01:31:59.722
You're not avoiding that
because you're fearful?

01:31:59.805 --> 01:32:01.265
Of course I'm not.

01:32:02.183 --> 01:32:03.976
Whose student am I, huh?

01:32:08.606 --> 01:32:11.901
Yeah. Well, look at me
lecturing to a higher player.

01:32:13.027 --> 01:32:14.028
[sighs]

01:32:14.111 --> 01:32:16.739
[announcer] Lee Chang-ho 7-dan
wins a no-count win

01:32:16.822 --> 01:32:19.033
and succeeds defending his title
of Daewang.

01:32:19.116 --> 01:32:21.744
He has 19 consecutive competition wins…

01:32:21.827 --> 01:32:26.165
What matters is how many consecutive wins
Lee Chang-ho gets, you know what I mean?

01:32:26.249 --> 01:32:28.251
[announcer] The Paewang
will be held in 15 days…

01:32:28.334 --> 01:32:31.712
[scoffs] You don't have to watch
to know Lee will win three to zero.

01:32:31.796 --> 01:32:34.257
-Cho Hoon-hyun is a has-been now.
-[laughs]

01:32:34.340 --> 01:32:36.425
[announcer] Cho 9-dan,
who's been going through a slump

01:32:36.509 --> 01:32:38.761
won through a variety
of preliminaries and finals,

01:32:38.844 --> 01:32:41.597
and now will challenge
Lee 7-dan once again.

01:32:41.681 --> 01:32:42.765
Lee 7-dan…

01:32:43.766 --> 01:32:44.642
[door closes]

01:32:45.560 --> 01:32:47.144
-Hello. [chuckles]
-You're here.

01:32:47.228 --> 01:32:48.646
-We're all done.
-Okay.

01:32:49.188 --> 01:32:51.107
-Hey, he's all mic'd up, yes?
-Yes.

01:32:51.190 --> 01:32:52.608
[chuckles]

01:32:52.692 --> 01:32:55.695
Champion Cho.
You can skip this if you want you.

01:32:56.612 --> 01:32:57.446
Should I?

01:32:58.531 --> 01:33:01.534
-Huh?
-[laughs] I'm joking.

01:33:01.617 --> 01:33:04.287
It's time I did one. It's been a while.

01:33:04.954 --> 01:33:06.372
Come on. [chuckles]

01:33:08.833 --> 01:33:10.418
First of all, congratulations.

01:33:10.501 --> 01:33:14.755
You were voted
the most popular Go player… [chuckles]

01:33:14.839 --> 01:33:15.798
…by the fans.

01:33:15.881 --> 01:33:16.882
How do you feel about it?

01:33:16.966 --> 01:33:21.262
If I knew it'd be like this,
I would have lost much sooner. [chuckles]

01:33:21.345 --> 01:33:24.056
When I was champion, I was hated so much.

01:33:24.140 --> 01:33:25.766
[both laugh]

01:33:25.850 --> 01:33:31.480
Well, the records show
you've played 110 matches last year alone.

01:33:31.564 --> 01:33:34.567
You've been playing practically
once every three days,

01:33:34.650 --> 01:33:37.570
including all the preliminaries
and the finals.

01:33:37.653 --> 01:33:41.240
In the past, you must have gotten used
to waiting as the defending champion.

01:33:41.949 --> 01:33:42.908
It's been rough.

01:33:43.409 --> 01:33:44.410
[smacks lips]

01:33:45.036 --> 01:33:49.415
Although, it makes the match
more exhilarating when a single…

01:33:49.498 --> 01:33:52.293
[smacks lips] …loss could send
you down that cliff.

01:33:52.376 --> 01:33:53.628
Fun, in a way.

01:33:53.711 --> 01:33:56.339
It was refreshing going
against those young rookies too.

01:33:58.799 --> 01:34:01.218
Lately, Lee Chang-ho 7-dan is on a roll.

01:34:01.302 --> 01:34:04.096
They say you're not a professional
until you lose to him.

01:34:04.180 --> 01:34:06.474
Let's end the interview
with your intentions.

01:34:07.016 --> 01:34:11.312
Any messages for Lee 7-dan,
your student and opponent in the final?

01:34:12.021 --> 01:34:15.274
[breathes deeply]

01:34:16.734 --> 01:34:19.695
Ah, Lee Chang-ho, he's my opponent.

01:34:21.656 --> 01:34:24.408
And even if I have to go against him,

01:34:25.284 --> 01:34:27.286
I plan on giving it my absolute best.

01:34:27.870 --> 01:34:31.957
[smacks lips] It's now my turn
to challenge him as he once did me.

01:34:32.541 --> 01:34:34.543
[anticipatory music playing]

01:34:41.050 --> 01:34:42.301
CHO HOON-HYUN RETURNS!

01:34:43.511 --> 01:34:45.054
[stones clattering]

01:34:45.137 --> 01:34:46.097
[stone clacks on board]

01:34:46.180 --> 01:34:48.432
[stones clattering]

01:34:48.516 --> 01:34:50.059
[music continues]

01:35:02.863 --> 01:35:04.073
[stones clattering]

01:35:05.825 --> 01:35:07.159
[stones clattering]

01:35:07.243 --> 01:35:10.246
31ST PAEWANG CUP CHALLENGE MATCH
LAST ROUND

01:35:10.329 --> 01:35:12.790
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS LEE CHANG-HO 7-DAN

01:35:13.332 --> 01:35:14.875
-[stone clacks on board]
-[timer clicks]

01:35:15.459 --> 01:35:17.002
-[stone clacks on board]
-[timer clicks]

01:35:19.004 --> 01:35:20.005
[timer clicks]

01:35:21.507 --> 01:35:22.425
[timer clicks]

01:35:24.760 --> 01:35:25.678
[timer clicks]

01:35:26.220 --> 01:35:27.138
[timer clicks]

01:35:28.973 --> 01:35:30.015
[stone clacks on board]

01:35:30.599 --> 01:35:31.600
[stone clacks on board]

01:35:32.977 --> 01:35:33.978
[timer clicks]

01:35:34.770 --> 01:35:37.815
This is the final game,
and both sides have two wins each,

01:35:37.898 --> 01:35:40.067
I was thinking the game
would begin in a cautious manner,

01:35:40.151 --> 01:35:42.862
but it's going extremely quickly,

01:35:42.945 --> 01:35:46.866
and the opening so far
is the same as the fourth match.

01:35:46.949 --> 01:35:48.451
Like they've choreographed their moves.

01:35:48.534 --> 01:35:51.328
It's very heated,
with neither of them backing down.

01:35:51.871 --> 01:35:54.498
They're both shouting
their way of Go is correct.

01:35:54.582 --> 01:35:58.878
[moderator] Lee Chang-ho 7-dan
is known as "The God of Calculation."

01:35:58.961 --> 01:36:02.965
Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan won
the very first two matches

01:36:03.048 --> 01:36:07.219
but lost the next two, and is now
standing at the edge of a cliff.

01:36:07.303 --> 01:36:10.848
The matches between the once student
and teacher continue in this pattern,

01:36:10.931 --> 01:36:14.685
with comeback wins now a signature
of Lee Chang-ho 7-dan's.

01:36:14.769 --> 01:36:19.607
[Gi-cheol] Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan's challenge
is to keep his composure 'til the end.

01:36:19.690 --> 01:36:20.649
[music continues]

01:36:26.322 --> 01:36:27.740
[moderator] Cho 9-dan's interesting.

01:36:28.324 --> 01:36:31.035
It's customary to take
and strengthen right here.

01:36:31.118 --> 01:36:33.329
Cho 9-dan placed his stone here.

01:36:34.038 --> 01:36:37.208
Hasn't Cho 9-dan's Go become
much sharper and acute

01:36:37.291 --> 01:36:39.418
since he's bounced back
from hitting rock bottom?

01:36:39.502 --> 01:36:42.838
His new nickname is "The God of War."

01:36:42.922 --> 01:36:47.218
[Gi-cheol] From that perspective, it seems
Cho 9-dan is planning to incite a fight.

01:36:47.802 --> 01:36:49.553
How will Lee 7-dan respond?

01:36:51.347 --> 01:36:54.308
[moderator] Oh, Lee 7-dan makes a hit!

01:36:54.391 --> 01:36:55.768
He's capturing.

01:36:55.851 --> 01:36:59.772
He doesn't seem to have any intention
to compromise. Unusual.

01:36:59.855 --> 01:37:02.316
It doesn't seem Cho 9-dan
expected this either.

01:37:02.399 --> 01:37:04.485
[anticipatory music continues]

01:37:16.831 --> 01:37:17.665
[stones clattering]

01:37:20.501 --> 01:37:25.089
Lee Chang-ho 7-dan strikes back
against Cho 9-dan's wave of attacks.

01:37:26.507 --> 01:37:27.341
[stones clatter]

01:37:27.925 --> 01:37:29.677
Cho 9-dan shakes up the center.

01:37:30.594 --> 01:37:33.722
It doesn't seem like Lee Chang-ho
will have to rise to the attack.

01:37:37.643 --> 01:37:41.105
Wow, Lee Chang-ho jumping in!

01:37:41.730 --> 01:37:44.316
They don't dare move their eyes
from the board.

01:37:44.400 --> 01:37:46.569
All they care about is the battle!

01:37:47.278 --> 01:37:49.572
Neither the teacher nor the student

01:37:49.655 --> 01:37:52.950
will give an inch
when it comes to the match.

01:37:53.033 --> 01:37:55.703
[music intensifies]

01:38:07.339 --> 01:38:09.383
This battle is truly chilling.

01:38:09.925 --> 01:38:12.386
They're fighting
like they're mortal enemies.

01:38:16.557 --> 01:38:19.560
Lee Chang-ho 7-dan is deep in thought.

01:38:20.227 --> 01:38:24.732
He's probably running tens of thousands
of possible sequences in his head.

01:38:24.815 --> 01:38:26.817
[music continues]

01:38:42.458 --> 01:38:43.584
[stones clattering]

01:38:46.879 --> 01:38:49.798
Oh, Lee Chang-ho suddenly
makes a sharp jab.

01:38:50.382 --> 01:38:52.551
Cho 9-dan has to be aching.

01:38:53.594 --> 01:38:56.931
Overall, the white
seems to be at an advantage.

01:38:57.014 --> 01:38:58.807
What are you thinking, Nam 9-dan?

01:38:58.891 --> 01:39:02.269
Champion Cho is starting fights
here and there,

01:39:03.437 --> 01:39:05.397
but Chan-ho's walls are just too thick.

01:39:05.481 --> 01:39:07.775
[Gi-cheol] It seems
Lee Chang-ho 7-dan is ahead

01:39:07.858 --> 01:39:11.111
by three and a half
or four and a half points so far.

01:39:11.195 --> 01:39:15.616
[moderator] Yes. This intense match
is entering its final endgame.

01:39:16.158 --> 01:39:18.535
If Lee Chang-ho 7-dan wins today,

01:39:18.619 --> 01:39:22.331
he'll become the second winner
of all cups, following his teacher.

01:39:22.414 --> 01:39:25.334
Lee Chang-ho 7-dan is almost there.

01:39:27.544 --> 01:39:28.879
[stones clattering]

01:39:30.255 --> 01:39:33.634
Oh, is he making a counterattack
in this situation?

01:39:34.176 --> 01:39:36.971
Is Cho 9-dan planning
to capture in this area?

01:39:37.054 --> 01:39:39.056
[sucks teeth] It won't be easy.

01:39:39.556 --> 01:39:42.142
It's Lee Chang-ho he's facing, after all.

01:39:42.851 --> 01:39:44.311
His defense is strong.

01:39:44.395 --> 01:39:46.605
It's Lee Chang-ho. A good position?

01:39:46.689 --> 01:39:50.275
Oh yes, he's staged a defense
and attacked a vital spot.

01:39:50.359 --> 01:39:51.235
[sucks teeth]

01:39:51.318 --> 01:39:53.862
It's very Lee Chang-ho.

01:39:55.823 --> 01:39:57.616
[moderator] Cho 9-dan
is now on the defensive.

01:39:57.700 --> 01:40:00.369
How will he get out
of this difficult situation?

01:40:00.452 --> 01:40:01.453
[Hoon-hyun exhales]

01:40:01.537 --> 01:40:05.457
[moderator] Cho 9-dan has never once been
at an advantage during this game.

01:40:05.541 --> 01:40:07.543
[anticipatory music continues]

01:40:08.669 --> 01:40:10.671
[stones clattering]

01:40:19.596 --> 01:40:23.058
Oh, what was that move?
Did that make any sense?

01:40:23.142 --> 01:40:25.811
[Pro Baek] What?
He's going to jump more here?

01:40:25.894 --> 01:40:28.105
Whoa, it's too reckless.

01:40:28.188 --> 01:40:29.940
There is nothing supporting it.

01:40:31.316 --> 01:40:32.735
[stones clattering]

01:40:40.826 --> 01:40:43.454
[moderator]
Oh, Lee Chang-oh 7-dan retreated.

01:40:44.288 --> 01:40:48.792
I think it'd be better to bend here
and capture one point, instead, right?

01:40:49.585 --> 01:40:50.753
What does that do?

01:40:52.921 --> 01:40:56.550
Is there perhaps something more
to Cho 9-dan's move?

01:40:57.676 --> 01:40:58.635
I'm perplexed.

01:40:58.719 --> 01:41:01.722
What are they up to?
There's something else going on.

01:41:02.347 --> 01:41:04.349
[contemplative music playing]

01:41:06.518 --> 01:41:09.354
[Hoon-hyun] Vital points are painful.

01:41:11.565 --> 01:41:16.278
The points where once you get hit,
you can't move and can only gasp.

01:41:19.573 --> 01:41:21.575
More stones on the board mingling,

01:41:22.826 --> 01:41:24.369
result in more vital points.

01:41:26.288 --> 01:41:28.791
My vital point is

01:41:30.209 --> 01:41:31.710
my opponent's vital point.

01:41:35.214 --> 01:41:37.174
-Wait just a minute.
-[moderator] Okay.

01:41:37.716 --> 01:41:39.301
I see it. It's complete genius.

01:41:40.177 --> 01:41:42.596
Black falls here, white does an atari,

01:41:42.679 --> 01:41:44.890
black connects,
then the white extends here.

01:41:45.474 --> 01:41:48.977
And in the end,
black inevitably gets the initiative.

01:41:49.061 --> 01:41:51.605
It's an exquisite victory bid
by Cho 9-dan.

01:41:51.688 --> 01:41:54.358
The teacher is finally twisting
the student's arm!

01:41:54.942 --> 01:41:58.403
If this works, Cho 9-dan
might actually turn the game around.

01:41:59.404 --> 01:42:01.031
[Gi-cheol] It takes two to play Go.

01:42:02.616 --> 01:42:06.662
A single genius player can't create
a good game of Go by himself.

01:42:06.745 --> 01:42:08.288
[tense music playing]

01:42:08.372 --> 01:42:12.209
This match
is one that will go down in history.

01:42:25.180 --> 01:42:27.307
[moderator] Lee Chang-ho bends
on the left side.

01:42:28.267 --> 01:42:29.768
Cho 9-dan blocks decisively.

01:42:29.852 --> 01:42:31.854
[music continues]

01:42:36.900 --> 01:42:39.153
[stone cracking]

01:42:43.782 --> 01:42:46.785
Oh-oh-oh, the stone statue
just winced, oh my!

01:42:46.869 --> 01:42:48.871
Lee Chang-ho is human after all!

01:42:48.954 --> 01:42:50.289
[stone clacks on board]

01:42:52.082 --> 01:42:52.916
Huh?

01:42:53.667 --> 01:42:55.669
[anticipatory music playing]

01:42:58.797 --> 01:43:01.091
[stones clattering]

01:43:31.205 --> 01:43:32.623
[stones clattering]

01:43:50.390 --> 01:43:51.642
[exhales]

01:43:51.725 --> 01:43:53.352
Lee Chang-ho resigns!

01:43:53.435 --> 01:43:57.356
Cho Hoon-hyun just blocked
Lee Chang-ho from a grand slam!

01:43:57.439 --> 01:43:58.732
Cho Hoon-hyun has won!

01:43:59.441 --> 01:44:03.737
Cho Hoon-hyun, who rose again and again
after 15 losses,

01:44:03.820 --> 01:44:07.741
finally leaves the hellish tunnel
that is Lee Chang-ho!

01:44:08.784 --> 01:44:13.163
Cho 9-dan becomes the Paewang
and escapes champion title exile!

01:44:13.247 --> 01:44:14.957
-[laughs]
-[moderator] Everyone!

01:44:15.040 --> 01:44:16.792
We welcome back the King!

01:44:16.875 --> 01:44:18.710
[all cheering]

01:44:18.794 --> 01:44:20.128
[cameras clicking]

01:44:20.212 --> 01:44:22.214
[music continues]

01:45:03.922 --> 01:45:04.756
WINNER

01:45:15.517 --> 01:45:20.314
29TH PAEWANG CHALLENGE WINNER

01:45:24.901 --> 01:45:28.113
[music fades]

01:45:28.947 --> 01:45:30.407
Have a safe journey back.

01:45:32.159 --> 01:45:33.243
Oh, here.

01:45:33.910 --> 01:45:34.745
Here, uh…

01:45:34.828 --> 01:45:37.247
Well, it didn't feel right
throwing it out.

01:45:37.331 --> 01:45:39.249
It's still usable. Here.

01:45:42.961 --> 01:45:44.504
[breathes deeply]

01:45:46.006 --> 01:45:47.382
TAXI

01:45:47.966 --> 01:45:51.970
Cut, throw-in, then bend,

01:45:52.846 --> 01:45:55.223
atari, then cover…

01:45:57.225 --> 01:45:58.226
[sighs]

01:46:19.831 --> 01:46:21.750
GO IS FINDING AN ANSWER
WHEN THERE ARE NO ANSWERS

01:46:24.669 --> 01:46:29.174
GO IS A FIGHT AGAINST YOURSELF
JULY 1964, CHO HOON-HYUN

01:46:29.925 --> 01:46:31.134
[chuckles softly]

01:46:36.765 --> 01:46:41.478
NOVEMBER 16, 1998
42ND GUKSU CUP EVE EVENT

01:46:42.145 --> 01:46:43.855
[Pro Cheon] Now,
let's wrap up the pictures

01:46:43.939 --> 01:46:45.357
and start the press conference.

01:46:45.440 --> 01:46:49.611
If the reporters could all please move
to their designated seats.

01:46:52.447 --> 01:46:57.035
First, the Guksu title has come
to represent you in a way,

01:46:57.119 --> 01:46:59.746
and so you must be feeling very emotional.

01:46:59.830 --> 01:47:00.956
You get a title,

01:47:02.165 --> 01:47:05.210
and can have it taken from you.
That's how it goes, right?

01:47:05.293 --> 01:47:06.920
Or it could be my age.

01:47:07.629 --> 01:47:11.341
But I'm more interested in…

01:47:12.467 --> 01:47:15.512
leaving behind a legacy game record
in my name.

01:47:15.595 --> 01:47:18.265
Cho 9-dan, you've been
on winning streak recently.

01:47:18.932 --> 01:47:20.642
What is your secret formula?

01:47:21.977 --> 01:47:23.145
[sighs] Well…

01:47:24.604 --> 01:47:25.647
Uh…

01:47:25.730 --> 01:47:30.277
Well, don't they say
the, uh, sun shines the brightest

01:47:30.360 --> 01:47:32.696
right before it begins to set?

01:47:34.364 --> 01:47:37.617
I expect it will be subsiding
sometime soon. [chuckles]

01:47:37.701 --> 01:47:39.661
What's your take, Lee 9-dan ?

01:47:39.744 --> 01:47:41.329
[people chuckling]

01:47:41.413 --> 01:47:44.124
He definitely stopped making mistakes
in the closing

01:47:44.207 --> 01:47:45.375
ever since he stopped smoking.

01:47:45.459 --> 01:47:47.169
Smoking must have been the problem.

01:47:47.252 --> 01:47:48.420
[all laugh]

01:47:48.503 --> 01:47:49.838
[reporter] Ha! Thank you.

01:47:51.006 --> 01:47:55.927
Uh, finally, do either of you have
a map in your mind for tomorrow's match?

01:47:56.511 --> 01:47:57.345
Hmm…

01:47:58.930 --> 01:48:01.391
Chang-ho's gotten a taste
for comeback wins,

01:48:02.100 --> 01:48:03.977
so he let me have the first round,

01:48:05.437 --> 01:48:08.815
but now that we're going for it,
I'll make tomorrow's match a lesson.

01:48:08.899 --> 01:48:10.025
[chuckles]

01:48:11.651 --> 01:48:14.237
I think that the one match
was lesson enough.

01:48:14.321 --> 01:48:15.405
[inhales deeply]

01:48:16.198 --> 01:48:19.618
Many are rooting
for my seonsaengnim Cho's victory,

01:48:20.285 --> 01:48:25.790
though I am not planning to give him
the championship title so easily either.

01:48:27.792 --> 01:48:30.003
[breathes deeply]

01:48:30.086 --> 01:48:32.088
[inspirational music playing]

01:48:50.440 --> 01:48:52.275
[Hoon-hyun] Chang-ho, you again?

01:48:55.028 --> 01:48:56.196
[Chang-ho] Yes, seonsaengnim.

01:49:00.784 --> 01:49:02.410
[Hoon-hyun] Ha, what can you do?

01:49:03.286 --> 01:49:04.704
This is the match.

01:49:11.753 --> 01:49:17.676
MUSHIM: TO EMPTY OUT ONE'S HEART

01:49:17.759 --> 01:49:18.969
[stones clatter]

01:49:23.848 --> 01:49:29.771
SEONG-EUI: TO GIVE ALL ONE'S HEART

01:49:29.854 --> 01:49:31.398
[music continues]

01:49:42.909 --> 01:49:43.910
[stone clacks on board]

01:49:44.661 --> 01:49:46.079
[stones clattering]

01:49:47.789 --> 01:49:49.791
[music continues]

01:49:51.793 --> 01:49:53.795
[birds chirping]

01:50:19.321 --> 01:50:21.323
[inspirational music continues]

01:50:23.658 --> 01:50:24.492
NOVEMBER 17, 1998

01:50:24.576 --> 01:50:26.661
CHO HOON-HYUN TAKES BACK
THE GUKSU CHAMPION TITLE,

01:50:26.745 --> 01:50:28.872
WHICH WAS HIS SYMBOL,
FROM LEE CHANG-HO AFTER FIVE YEARS

01:50:28.955 --> 01:50:30.206
THE FIRST SNOW FELL THAT DAY

01:50:36.504 --> 01:50:39.299
LEE CHANG-HO RULED AT THE TOP
OF THE INTERNATIONAL GO SCENE FOR 15 YEARS

01:50:39.382 --> 01:50:40.675
FOLLOWING HIS TEACHER'S FOOTSTEPS

01:50:40.759 --> 01:50:43.011
AND IS STILL CONSIDERED
AS THE STRONGEST PLAYER IN HISTORY

01:50:47.057 --> 01:50:49.684
THE TEACHER AND THE STUDENT

01:50:49.768 --> 01:50:53.563
ARE STILL PLAYING

01:50:53.647 --> 01:50:55.649
[inspirational music continues]

01:54:25.316 --> 01:54:26.609
[music fades]
